ritise commitments against the domain strategy using quantitative and qualitative evidence, and share your trade-offs internally and externally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure that any partner-specific integrations have longevity within our platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engage directly with enterprise partners and prospects - scope requirements, negotiate delivery, prioritise.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with dwpbank counterparts on joint product opportunities, translating between two organisations with different ways of working.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Propose forward-looking solutions that outlive the immediate ask, rather than one-off fixes for the loudest partner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track market and regulatory developments in our space, and bring the insights back to the team.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>You’ll be successful in this role if:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have at least 2-3 years of product experience, independently shipping highly complex products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are comfortable with ambiguity - you can define a problem space, structure it, and move forward without waiting for someone else to hand you a spec.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You argue your position based on data and evidence, and iterate when the evidence changes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can express yourself in writing. Documentation, decisions, specs, partner comms - clear writing is a core part of the job.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You use AI tools in your day-to-day work and are comfortable pushing what they can do.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are professionally fluent in English and German.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in regulated fintech / brokerage or B2B environments is a plus!</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong