le="min-height:1.5em">AI search is changing how brands are discovered and chosen. People now ask ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude and Google’s AI answers what they used to search for, and AI assistants increasingly shape the journey from discovery to purchase. Winning customers now means winning over the AI systems that influence their decisions. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Peec AI is an AI search platform that helps marketing teams understand and improve how their brands are discovered, represented, and recommended. We show them where they stand, what’s shaping it, and where to act. Since launching in January 2025, Peec AI has passed $20M ARR and 4,000 paying customers. We’re a Series A company backed by 20VC and Singular, with 100+ people across our Berlin HQ and our New York office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Almost everything Peec shows a customer passes through a model at some point. We track brands, products, sentiment, citations and sources across millions of AI answers. Those answers change whenever a provider ships a new model and differ by country, language and prompt. Turning that into numbers customers can trust and act on is the core data science problem at Peec.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our data science team has grown fast, with AI-powered features shipping across the product. We're now growing the team further and need someone to lead it. You'll turn a group of strong individual contributors into a high-powered, fast-shipping team. You'll report directly to the CTO and lead a team of 7 data scientists. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leading people</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hire, onboard and grow the data science team. We're hiring several data scientists right now, and you'll shape who joins and how they ramp up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a team culture that matches our values: a high bar for quality, full ownership of outcomes, and kindness towards each other</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead and inspire the team through regular 1:1s, actionable feedback and clear career paths</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leading the technical work</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the technical direction and roadmap for data science, together with product and engineering leadership, and decide what the team works on and what it doesn't</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own quality in production with strong operational excellence and reproducibility across the ML lifecycle</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive innovation by investing in scalable machine learning data infrastructure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay close to the work: review designs and code, and step in hands-on when it matters</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent data science to leadership and customers</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we're looking for</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8+ years in data science or machine learning, including 3+ years managing data scientists or ML engineers as direct reports, ideally at a high-growth startup or an established tech company</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of building great teams: hiring well, developing people, and creating the standards and rituals that make a team more than the sum of its individuals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience taking ML products from research to production, and building the practices that keep them reliable: evaluation, monitoring, reproducibility</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A solid understanding of LLMs and strong instincts for measurement and statistics when outputs are noisy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical depth to review architecture and modeling decisions, ideally in cloud-native environments (GCP a plus)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear communication with executives, engineers and customers, including being honest about uncertainty</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good judgment under ambiguity, and the ownership to deliver outcomes despite blockers</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Our stack</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">A standard Python and SQL stack on GCP. We work with all the major LLM providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Perplexity) as well as open-weight models.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Bonus points</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contributions to open-source projects or ML tooling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Public side or research projects that show technical depth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Publications or talks at ML or AI conferences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founder experience or senior technical leadership at a high-growth startup</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A defining leadership role with real impact and ownership at one of Europe's fastest-growing Series A startups</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular team events and off-sites</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aggressive equity compensation package</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid dinner &amp; Uber home when working late</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The most beautiful office space and work environment in Berlin</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><hr><p>Compensation: €120K – €160K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • €120K – €160K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/peec-ai/head-of-data-science-berlin-119191","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793936413},{"slug":"growth-engineer-berlin-360504","company_name":"Peec AI","title":"Growth Engineer","description":"<h2>About Peec AI</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI search is changing how brands are discovered and chosen. People now ask ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude and Google’s AI answers what they used to search for, and AI assistants increasingly shape the journey from discovery to purchase. Winning customers now means winning over the AI systems that influence their decisions. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Peec AI is an AI search platform that helps marketing teams understand and improve how their brands are discovered, represented, and recommended. We show them where they stand, what’s shaping it, and where to act. Since launching in January 2025, Peec AI has passed $20M ARR and 4,000 paying customers. We’re a Series A company backed by 20VC and Singular, with 100+ people across our Berlin HQ and our New York office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are hiring a Fullstack Engineer for our Growth team. You will run experiments across the whole self-serve journey: from the moment someone first hears of Peec AI to the day they renew, refer a friend or leave. That covers the website, signup, pricing and checkout, the trial and onboarding. It also covers the moments in the product where we ask people to do something, like connect a tool, invite a teammate or upgrade. You can work on any of these, and we decide together where the focus goes each month or quarter.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You come up with the hypothesis, design the experiment and discuss it with the team. Then you run the rest of the loop yourself: build it, instrument it, ship it behind a flag, read the result and write down what happened.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You report to the VP of Growth and work with our Growth PM, our growth engineer, and the marketing and design teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Go after big swings. We size every idea first and look for changes that could move a funnel step by 30 to 40 percentage points. It is fine if most of them fail.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and improve the experimentation infrastructure. Feature flags, assignment at the account level, exposure logged when someone becomes eligible, outcomes recorded on the server, and holdouts we read.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep conversion data accurate. Event design, funnel definitions and readouts the team can rely on.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own what you ship after launch. You watch it, read the result on the date you set, and decide whether we keep it, change it or remove it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build internal tools that let the team run more experiments with less manual work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we're looking for</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have run growth experiments end to end. You formed the hypothesis, designed the test, built it and read the result. Not advised on them, not analysed someone else's.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You write production code today. Strong React and TypeScript on the frontend, comfortable in Node.js and databases on the backend. Our stack is React, Node.js and Next.js.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You know what your volume can detect. You can size a test, say how long it needs to run, and tell us when a result is not readable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">SQL and analytics fluency. Funnels, cohorts, event design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">B2B SaaS experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You ship with Claude Code, Cursor or equivalent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product judgement. You can tell which changes need a test, which can ship without one, and which are not worth building.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product taste. You care about how the things you ship look and feel. You can turn an idea into a screen that belongs in our product, and you know when to bring in our design team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Bonus points</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You set up an experimentation practice from scratch and grew it into a regular part of how the team works.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product-led growth experience. Onboarding, activation, paywalls, pricing, checkout.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Acquisition experience. Website and signup experiments, SEO or paid funnels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experiments on low-volume B2B funnels, where only big changes are readable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experimentation platforms and feature flags. Statsig, GrowthBook, PostHog, or your own.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Billing and subscriptions. Stripe or similar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You founded a company, or you were an early engineer at one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Side projects and experiments you can show us.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exciting and challenging work with real impact and ownership at one of Europe's fastest-growing Series A startups</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular team events and off-sites</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aggressive equity compensation package</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid Dinner &amp; Uber home when working late</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The most beautiful office space and work environment in Berlin</p></li></ul><hr><p>Compensation: €100K – €130K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • €100K – €130K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/e