e="min-height:1.5em">Zusammenarbeit mit jungem Management </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Moderne, attraktive Praxis, die zum Austausch einlädt und das Wohlbefinden fördert </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Junges, dynamisches Team, das etwas bewegen will </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>IHRE AUFGABEN</strong> </h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sie unterstützen im Praxisalltag am Empfang, im Labor und bei der Behandlung </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sie unterstützen bei Dokumentation und Abrechnung (EBM, GoÄ) </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sie unterstützen das Recall-Management und Patiententelefon </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sie unterstützen beim Beschaffungsmanagement </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">(<strong>falls NäPa/Verah/Eva</strong>) Sie betreuen Ihre Patienten durch regelmäßige Hausbesuche und Heimbesuche </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>IHR PROFIL</strong> </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bei uns zählen Charakter und Menschlichkeit mehr als Skills &amp; Erfahrung.</strong> Auch wenn Sie nicht alle Punkte des Anforderungsprofils erfüllen, bitten wir Sie, uns Ihre Bewerbung zu senden. Schließlich können wir alles beibringen, wenn der Charakter und die Einstellung stimmt! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Um Teil unseres Teams zu werden, bringen Sie idealerweise mit: </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lebensfrohe und offene Natur </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Verantwortungsbewusstes und respektvolles Auftreten </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hohes Maß an Selbstorganisation und Zuverlässigkeit </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Berufserfahrung in einer Praxis im hausärztlichen Bereich oder als MFA bzw. in der Pflege </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leichtigkeit im Umgang mit digitalen Programmen </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deutschkenntnisse auf sehr gutem Niveau </p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">(Von Vorteil) abgeschlossene NäPa/Eva/Verah Ausbildung </p></li></ul><h1><strong>Über PraxisEins</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">PraxisEins ist ein staatlich unterstützter Gesundheitsversorger mit einem Fokus auf den Bereichen der hausärztlichen Versorgung, Diabetologie und Schmerztherapie.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Unsere Mission</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Versorgung sichern - Qualitätsmedizin gewährleisten. Als PraxisEins wollen wir die Primärversorgung zukunftsfähig machen – mit digitaler Unterstützung, klaren Prozessen und einem Umfeld, in dem Ärztinnen und Ärzte Medizin wieder mit Freude ausüben können!<br /><em><br />PraxisEins ist ein Arbeitgeber, der Chancengleichheit fördert und Vielfalt schätzt. Wir freuen uns über alle Bewerbungen und bearbeiten diese völlig unabhängig von Geschlecht, Religionszugehörigkeit, Hautfarbe, Herkunft, sexueller Orientierung, Alter, Familienstand oder Behindertenstatus. Zur besseren Lesbarkeit wird in dieser Stellenanzeige das generische Maskulinum verwendet.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/praxiseins/medizinische-fachangestellte-bochum-dahlhausen-289296","tags":["MFA"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Linden Dahlhausen","created_at":1793936412},{"slug":"remote-endear-product-designer-79201","company_name":"Eleve Talent","title":"Endear - Product Designer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location:</strong> Remote, US-based<br /><strong>Team:</strong> Product &amp; Design — IRL<br /><strong>Type:</strong> Full-Time, Employee<br /><strong>Compensation:</strong> $100K–$129K base<br /><strong>Target Start:</strong> January 2027 or earlier</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Our Story</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Endear, we’re building the modern CRM for retail teams — starting with the frontline.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our software helps retail teams build stronger customer relationships through thoughtful, intuitive technology. From clienteling and customer capture to appointments and in-store experiences, Endear gives brands the tools they need to create more personal interactions and drive measurable growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work with brands like Allbirds, Reformation, and Alo Yoga, and we’re continuing to evolve Endear into an increasingly AI-first product built around how modern retail teams actually work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Position Overview</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a Product Designer to join our IRL (in real life) team, which owns the in-store side of Endear — including appointments, events, customer check-ins, and the administrative experiences behind those workflows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll design for store associates and managers running clienteling day to day, as well as admin users who help shape how those teams operate and manage their workflows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role, you’ll own features and projects from understanding the problem through research, testing, iteration, and production-ready design, while partnering closely with our Head of Product Design on vision and direction.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The IRL roadmap is early. Many of these features don’t exist yet, so you’ll be defining problems through research before designing solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is well suited for someone comfortable creating clarity when the solution isn’t obvious.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>What You’ll Accomplish</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In your first 6 months, you’ll…</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take ownership of IRL features from discovery through production-ready design</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a strong understanding of how store associates, managers, and admin users work within Endear</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run research from early discovery through usability testing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design complete, accessible product experiences, including loading, empty, error, permission, and other key states.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with Product and Engineering to shape solutions early in the process</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use customer insight and data to inform design decisions and iteration</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In your first year, you’ll…</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build deeper ownership across the IRL product</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver product experiences that improve how retail teams manage clienteling and in-store workflows</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a strong rhythm of discovery, testing, and continuous learning</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strengthen your collaboration across Design, Product, and Engineering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrate clear user and business impact through the work you ship</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You’ll Thrive in This Role If…</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You enjoy taking ownership of a feature while collaborating closely on the broader vision and direction</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re comfortable with ambiguity and zero-to-one product work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You naturally think beyond the happy path and account for edge cases and complete product states</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You care about creating accessible experiences and solving the right problem, not just creating polished UI</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You enjoy working closely with Product and Engineering throughout the design process</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re comfortable using research, data, and customer feedback to guide decisions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You move quickly, seek feedback, and iterate based on what you learn</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re curious about designing for AI</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You Have Experience With</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2–5 years working in product design</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Independently owning features from discovery through implementation, with support on vision and direction</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Running user research from discovery through usability testing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translating broad or ambiguous problems into clear product solutions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working closely with Design, Product, and Engineering teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Designing complex, accessible workflows and accounting for loading, empty, error, and permission states</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Using qualitative and quantitative data to inform design decisions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building within established design patterns while knowing when something needs to evolve</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Using AI tools as part of your workflow and applying judgment to AI-generated output</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A portfolio that demonstrates strong product thinking and execution, and where you can articulate the impact of your work, with data where you had access to it</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Align With What We Value</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Endear, we live by five core principles. Here’s how they translate into what we’re looking for in this role:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer First:</strong> You start by understanding the people using the product, run thoughtful research, and use what you learn to shape better experiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Take Ownership: </strong>You take responsibility for your features, follow through on the details, and care about the quality of what ships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enable Autonomy:</strong> You communicate clearly, collaborate early, and give Product and Engineering the context they need to make strong decisions together.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Under Promise, Over Deliver:</strong> You set realistic expectations, think through the details, and deliver complete, production-ready work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Innovate &amp; Deliver Value Quickly:</strong> You’re comfortable experimenting, using AI and other tools thoughtfully, and moving quickly without sacrificing sound product judgment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>About the Team</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Endear’s product organization is structured across three product teams: AI, IRL, and Core Flows, with one designer dedicated to each.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the IRL designer, you’ll work closely with a Product Manager and 2–3 Engineers while also being part of Endear’s three-person design team. You’ll report to the Head of Product Design, who will provide vision, direction, mentorship, and support as you grow in the role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll partner most closely with:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Head of Product Design: </strong>vision, direction, mentorship, feedback, and design leadership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Product Team:</strong> roadmap alignment, priorities, customer needs, and business context</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Engineering Team:</strong> feasibility, implementation, and iteration</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll have access to mentorship, an education budget, and support around Endear’s AI processes to help you continue developing your craft and expanding how you use AI in your work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a small team with big ambitions — collaborative, customer-obsessed, and deeply excited about the problems we’re solving in retail.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Our Hiring Process</strong></h3><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruiter Screen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Behavioral Interview with the Hiring Manager</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team Portfolio Review with Design, Product + Engineering</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final leadership conversation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offer 🎉</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Compensation &amp; Benefits</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Base Salary: $100K–$129K</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fully remote, US-based team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive healthcare (medical, dental, vision)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Co-working or home office stipend</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible PTO and unlimited vacation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Education and learning support</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Opportunity to shape foundational product work in a transformative industry</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Location: This role is remote and US-based. Our full team comes together for an all-team standup every Monday at 8:00 AM Pacific, so you’ll need to be available at that time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>Apply Even If You Don’t Check Every Box</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">If this role excites you but you’re unsure if you meet every requirement, reach out anyway. No retail or e-commerce background is required. We care about your product thinking, skills, motivation, and how you approach problems more than we do about perfect resumes.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/eleve-talent/remote-endear-product-designer-79201","tags":["Endear"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Remote","created_at":1793936412},{"slug":"customer-success-access-operations-specialist-berlin-465484","company_name":"AMBOSS","title":"Customer Success - Access Operations Specialist","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location</strong>: Berlin (Hybrid)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hi, we’re AMBOSS and we’re searching for a Customer Success - Access Operations Specialist to support our institutional customers and Sales team at AMBOSS.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About AMBOSS</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">AMBOSS is the copilot for medical professionals, empowering them to provide the best possible care through our learning and clinical decision support tool. Our team brings together care, innovative thinking, and cutting-edge AI medical technology. Our founders launched AMBOSS in 2012 with the goal of creating a tool they wished they had during medical school and clinical practice. Since then, we’ve grown to over 600 employees and are active in over 180 countries - primarily in Germany and the US. Our offices are located in Berlin, Cologne, New York, Cagliari and Cape Town.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Want to learn more about our culture? Watch our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gTPDn5XpeJg"> <u>video</u></a> to explore what makes us unique.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why can this position be exciting for you?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Institutions can only get value from AMBOSS if their users can reach it easily and know it’s available to them, and as our Customer Success - Access Operations Specialist, you are the person who makes that happen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll play a key role in ensuring our institutional partners unlock the full value of AMBOSS, helping embed it into daily clinical and teaching routines and strengthening user experience, retention, and growth. Reporting to the Head of Customer Success, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ronald-lattuf">Ronald</a>, you will help support our International and US customers and the respective Sales Managers, contributing to our revenue and internationalization company goals.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>You will:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manage, prioritize and effectively address requests</strong> from our B2B Sales Team and institutional administrators to support their license and trial launches, always keeping the experience and value our users get from AMBOSS at the center.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Consult internal Sales stakeholders and institutional customers </strong>on the best access method for AMBOSS, using active listening and targeted discovery questions to understand each institution’s needs, explaining complex concepts simply for each audience, and making clear recommendations based on a solid understanding of the advantages and disadvantages of each option in the specific customer situation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Set up the agreed access methods for AMBOSS by following through on the technical details</strong> of the implementation with the institution’s IT team and our internal stakeholders, ensuring each access method is configured correctly and ready on time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the project management </strong>of complex access set-ups, such as single sign-on or licenses with multiple access methods, by aligning institutional IT teams, administrators, Engineering, and Sales on scope, timelines, and responsibilities, tracking progress against milestones, resolving blockers early, and guiding the set-up end to end through go-live.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Conduct in-depth analysis </strong>of customer adoption patterns, translating data into actionable insights and recommendations that support institutional success and long-term engagement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work closely with</strong> Engineering, Data, Sales, Marketing and other <strong>departments</strong> to jointly tackle difficult customer challenges and to continuously improve how we support sales and our customers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>You bring:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ideally you have a previous experience in customer success or customer support (1-2y or an internship) combined with a degree in Business Administration, Marketing, Management or a relevant field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are an outstanding communicator, both in writing and verbally. You can break down complex topics to their essence and communicate them appropriately based on your audience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are pragmatic and action-oriented. You work productively through a high volume of requests, focusing on timely, effective solutions rather than perfect ones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are decisive. You make well-reasoned decisions even when information is incomplete, can explain the thinking behind them, and continuously learn from mistakes by reflecting openly and adjusting your approach.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are able to build rapport with stakeholders across different countries and seniority levels through a mix of authenticity and openness, competence, and clear communication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a project management mindset and are able to independently organize your work to ensure you deliver in time and quality, even for more complex projects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You possess an analytical mindset and an affinity for numbers that allows you to interpret usage analytics and derive relevant insights for our customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have an eye for efficiency and contribute to continuously improving our internal processes and materials.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You enjoy:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fostering your growth mindset and continuously learning</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Persevering and staying motivated to achieve your goals even when challenges arise</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learning and growing based on feedback and coaching</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Benefits:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">AMBOSSians tell us that innovative work keeps them energized and employee benefits help them to feel appreciated and empowered. We invest in every AMBOSSian with our employee benefits package, crafted to support financial, physical, and mental health, and work-life harmony.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌴 <strong>Rest &amp; Time Off</strong> (30 paid vacation days, AMBOSS holiday, personal purpose day and more)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🥙 <strong>Food &amp; Office Comfort</strong> (Daily healthy breakfast &amp; lunch by in-house chef in Berlin HQ, AMBOSS daycare, work remotely from other office spaces in Cologne, Sardinia, Cape Town)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏃 <strong>Health, Fitness &amp; Mobility</strong> (Urban Sports Club – M plan, Fitbit Versa 3, Deutschland Ticket…)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check out the full list of benefits below:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://go.amboss.com/the-amboss-prescription-de"> <u>https://go.amboss.com/the-amboss-prescription-de</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe that diversity is a powerful driver of innovation and progress. That’s why we are committed to fostering an inclusive, respectful, and supportive environment where everyone—regardless of gender, age, ethnic or cultural background, religion, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity—is valued and given equal opportunity to thrive. We warmly welcome people of all backgrounds to help us fulfil our mission: empowering all medical professionals to provide the best possible care 🩺</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Even if you don’t meet every single point in the job description, we still encourage you to apply. We’d love to hear from you!</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/amboss/customer-success-access-operations-specialist-berlin-465484","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793936412},{"slug":"senior-financial-systems-architect-workday-berlin-84146","company_name":"AMBOSS","title":"Senior Financial Systems Architect - Workday","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Hi! We are AMBOSS and we are looking for a <strong>Financial Systems Architect</strong> to join our team, and shape the future of medical education with us!<br /><br /><strong>About AMBOSS</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AMBOSS is a dynamic learning and clinical decision support tool committed to empowering medical professionals  globally to deliver optimal care. Since our inception in 2012, we've harnessed cutting-edge technology to transform the way physicians acquire and apply scientific knowledge. Each AMBOSSian is passionate about being the champion of clinicians today - this motivates and unites us each day towards success. And what does success look like? When a clinician or med student tells us, “AMBOSS makes practicing medicine easier and enjoyable. I love what I do, and a big part is because of AMBOSS.”</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Want to learn more about our culture? Watch our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://youtu.be/gTPDn5XpeJg"><u> video</u></a><u> </u>to explore what makes us unique.</p><h2><br /><strong>Why Systems at AMBOSS?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">AMBOSS runs on a growing landscape of business systems: Workday as the ERP at the center, connected to Stripe, HubSpot, Pleo, Avalara, our banks, payroll and archiving. The Systems team, part of Data &amp; Systems, makes this landscape develop as a whole: every problem solved in the system where it belongs, and processes that run smoothly from order to cash and from purchase to payment. Our expertise is platform-independent: accounting logic, process design, integration patterns and systems thinking. Working side by side with Finance, Accounting, Commercial, Data and IT, we support AMBOSS in pursuing its mission: empowering medical professionals worldwide to provide the best possible care.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Why can this position be exciting for you?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are the technical owner of Workday Financials at AMBOSS: you take the tenant over from our implementation partner and run it. Some days that means a configuration fix before the close, other days the design of a new integration or the assessment of a new module.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are the expert and advisor for everything Workday. Our Business Systems Manager owns the roadmap, stakeholder coordination and partner management and works with you day to day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a senior individual contributor role: you build and own Workday the way a senior engineer owns a production system. It is not an administrator role with a ticket queue.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Where we are</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Workday Financials goes live in November 2026 as our ERP for three entities in Germany, the US and Italy. Around twelve integrations connect it to the rest of the landscape, and they are the most demanding part of it. You join during hypercare and the first closes in Workday, with the first year-end close and statutory audit ahead.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>You will:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the tenant technically.</strong> Configuration and business processes across record-to-report (General Ledger), procure-to-pay (Accounts Payable), order-to-cash (Accounts Receivable) and bank connectivity (Banking &amp; Settlement), the security model and the financial data model.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Take over from the implementation partner.</strong> Review, document and harden what was delivered, close the gaps and bring run responsibility in-house as early as possible after go-live. Where we still use consultants, you set the technical standard and review their work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own the Workday side of every integration.</strong> Design and build the EIBs, Core Connectors, Studio integrations, web services and RaaS reports behind each interface and agree the interface contracts with our Data Platform engineers, who build and run the pipelines around the tenant.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Advise Accounting and Finance.</strong> Translate requirements into system design, say clearly what Workday can and cannot do and advise where in the landscape a problem is best solved.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run it like a production system.</strong> Tier 2/3 support with root-cause fixes, testing discipline (unit, regression, UAT), the two Workday releases a year and a change log with configuration documentation. You enable the accounting stream leads who handle first-line questions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the reports, dashboards and calculated fields</strong> that Finance and leadership rely on, and make them self-serve where possible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Be the technical expert on expansions.</strong> HCM, treasury, automated VAT reporting and global payroll off DATEV: assess feasibility, design the solution and configure it.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>You bring:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Workday Financials depth.</strong> 5+ years hands-on, including at least one full implementation and the post-go-live ownership of a tenant (hypercare, first closes, releases).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Configuration expertise.</strong> Core modules (GL, AP, AR, Banking &amp; Settlement), the business process framework, configurable security and the financial data model (FDM, worktags).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reporting.</strong> Custom and matrix reports, calculated fields and BIRT.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Systems thinking.</strong> Experience connecting SaaS business systems (APIs, integration patterns) and the habit of thinking in end-to-end processes across tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Accounting understanding.</strong> Chart of accounts, period close, reconciliations and audit requirements.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Engineering mindset.</strong> Structured troubleshooting to the root cause, disciplined testing and documentation that others can use.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Communication.</strong> Excellent English: precise with engineers, plain with finance colleagues.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Nice to have:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience with Workday integration tooling: EIBs, Core Connectors, Studio, web services, RaaS and XSLT</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in German</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Workday Pro certification in Financials or Integrations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Multi-entity, multi-currency or multi-GAAP experience (IFRS alongside local GAAP); experience with tax and e-invoicing platforms such as Avalara</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accounting Center, Prism Analytics, Extend or Orchestrate</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A Workday consulting or CoE background</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A formal accounting background (degree, CPA or equivalent) or experience with internal controls and SOX in a Workday context</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>You enjoy:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Owning a system end to end.</strong> Taking over a freshly built tenant and knowing it better than anyone else in the company within months.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Depth you can explain.</strong> You do the hard configuration and integration work yourself, and you explain the result to accountants and engineers in language each of them understands.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Getting the details right where they matter.</strong> Financial systems punish sloppiness: a misconfigured business process or a broken integration shows up in the books. You can tell a load-bearing detail (audit trail, data integrity, reconciliations) from polish that can wait.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Working like an engineer.</strong> You bring testing, documentation and versioned change into Workday and use modern tooling, including AI assistants, to move faster. When a release or a new module moves the ground, you question your own setup first.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What success looks like after your first year:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The tenant runs without the implementation partner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The integrations run reliably through every month-end and year-end close: data lands in Workday without manual intervention, and monitoring catches failures before Accounting does.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The first year-end close and statutory audit in Workday are done with you answering the auditors' system questions, and two Workday releases are handled end to end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accounting and Finance treat you as the expert and advisor for everything Workday: requirements are shaped with you from the start, and your call on how a process should run in the system is the one they act on.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Benefits:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🌴 Rest &amp; Time Off</strong> (30 paid vacation days, AMBOSS holiday, personal purpose day and more)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🥙Food &amp; Office Comfort (</strong>Daily healthy breakfast &amp; lunch by in-house chef in Berlin HQ, AMBOSS daycare, work remotely from other office spaces in Cologne, Sardinia, Cape Town)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🏃 Health, Fitness &amp; Mobility</strong> (Urban Sports Club -M plan- , Fitbit Versa 3, Deutschland Ticket…)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Check out the full list of benefits below:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://go.amboss.com/the-amboss-prescription-de"><u>https://go.amboss.com/the-amboss-prescription-de</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe that diversity is a powerful driver of innovation and progress. That’s why we are committed to fostering an inclusive, respectful, and supportive environment where everyone—regardless of gender, age, ethnic or cultural background, religion, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity—is valued and given equal opportunity to thrive. We warmly welcome people of all backgrounds to help us fulfil our mission: empowering all medical professionals  to provide the best possible care  🩺</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Even if you don’t meet every single point in the job description, we still encourage you to apply. We’d love to hear from you!</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/amboss/senior-financial-systems-architect-workday-berlin-84146","tags":["General & Administration"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793936412},{"slug":"werkstudentin-finance-accounting-munchen-118498","company_name":"limehome","title":"Werkstudent:in Finance & Accounting (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Greif mit uns nach den Sternen!</strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Zur Unterstützung unseres Finance-Teams bei Limehome suchen wir eine:n motivierte:n Werkstudent:in Finance &amp; Accounting (m/w/d). Du unterstützt primär unser Accounting-Team im Tagesgeschäft und bei den Monatsabschlüssen und bekommst je nach Bedarf darüber hinaus Einblicke in weitere Finance-Themen wie Reporting, FP&amp;A und Prozessautomatisierung. So lernst du eine moderne, tech-getriebene Finanzfunktion in einem international wachsenden Unternehmen von Grund auf kennen und übernimmst früh Verantwortung.</span></p><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Als ‘Host with heart’ bist du für diese Themen verantwortlich:</strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Du unterstützt das Accounting-Team im Tagesgeschäft, zum Beispiel in der Kreditorenbuchhaltung (z. B. Rechnungserfassung, Kontenabstimmung, Belegmanagement).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Du hilfst bei vorbereitenden Tätigkeiten für die Monats- und Jahresabschlüsse mit.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Du unterstützt bei der Aufbereitung von Daten und Auswertungen, z. B. für Reportings oder Ad-hoc Anfragen.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Du wirkst an der Verbesserung und Automatisierung von Finance-Prozessen mit – inkl. dem Einsatz von Tools und KI.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Du übernimmst eigenständig je nach Bedarf kleinere Projekte und Ad-hoc-Aufgaben über den gesamten Finance-Bereich hinweg.</span></p></li></ul> <br> <p style="text-align:start;"><strong>Was Du brauchst, um mit uns nach den Sternen zu greifen:</strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Du bist eingeschriebene:r Student:in, idealerweise mit wirtschaftswissenschaftlichem Schwerpunkt (z. B. BWL, Finance, Accounting, Wirtschaftsinformatik).</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Du bringst eine sorgfältige, strukturierte und zuverlässige Arbeitsweise mit und arbeitest gerne mit Zahlen.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Du hast eine Affinität für Prozesse, Tools und Systeme und Interesse an Automatisierung und KI</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Du bist proaktiv, lernbereit und übernimmst gerne früh Verantwortung.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Du beherrschst Deutsch und Englisch sehr gut in Wort und Schrift.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Du kannst uns idealerweise für etwa 16-20 Stunden pro Woche unterstützen (flexibel in der Prüfungszeit).</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317"><span style="background-color:#ffffff">Darum wirst du deinen “Aufenthalt” bei uns lieben:</span></span></strong></p><ul><li><p><strong><span style="color:#5a5f72"><span style="background-color:#ffffff">Onboarding und Feedback:</span></span></strong><span style="color:#5a5f72"><span style="background-color:#ffffff"> Wir sorgen mit unserem gut durchdachten Onboarding-Prozess für einen reibungslosen Start. Regelmäßiges Feedback und Peer Reviews unterstützen dich zusätzlich in deiner Weiterentwicklung.&nbsp;</span></span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#5a5f72"><span style="background-color:#ffffff">OneTeam:</span></span></strong><span style="color:#5a5f72"><span style="background-color:#ffffff"> Eine offene Unternehmenskultur mit Team-Stand-ups, regelmäßigen All-Hands-Meetings und Firmenevents (Sommerparty, Wiesn,...).</span></span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#5a5f72"><span style="background-color:#ffffff">Alles für unsere Limehomies:</span></span></strong><span style="color:#5a5f72"><span style="background-color:#ffffff"> Bis zu 24 bezahlte Urlaubstage im Jahr, Rabatte bei Urban Sports Club, Unterstützung beim Thema psychische Gesundheit (Nilo.health), Staycations in einem unserer Limehomes und viele weitere Vorteile.</span></span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#5a5f72"><span style="background-color:#ffffff">Wettbewerbsfähiges Gehalt</span></span></strong><span style="color:#5a5f72"><span style="background-color:#ffffff">: Unsere faire Vergütung für Werkstudierende 15€ (Bachelor)/17€ (Master) / unser Praktikantengehalt von 2.550/1800 € ermöglichen dir einen komfortablen Lebensstil</span></span></p></li><li><p><strong><span style="color:#5a5f72"><span style="background-color:#ffffff">Kostenlose Getränke und Snacks:</span></span></strong><span style="color:#5a5f72"><span style="background-color:#ffffff"> Frisches Obst, gesunde Snacks und Schokolade sind genau wie Kaffee und Softdrinks zur freien Verfügung</span></span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>Über Limehome:</strong></p><p>Limehome ist ein führender, technologiebasierter Hospitality-Betreiber, der funktional gestaltete Designunterkünfte in ganz Europa anbietet. Durch den Einsatz seiner proprietären Technologie ermöglicht Limehome einen reibungslosen und komfortablen Aufenthalt mit einem nahtlosen digitalen Gästeerlebnis für Geschäfts- und Urlaubsreisende. Gegründet im Jahr 2018, beschäftigt Limehome heute über 300 Mitarbeitende  und zählt über 10.000 Limehome Apartments und Hotelzimmer in 150 Städten in 13 europäischen Ländern. </p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/limehome/werkstudentin-finance-accounting-munchen-118498","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Student college","internship"],"location":"München, Bayern, Germany","created_at":1793935910},{"slug":"lead-engineer-gn-at-ai-venture-berlin-78333","company_name":"atlantic.vc","title":"Lead Engineer (gn) @ AI Venture, Berlin","description":"<p><strong>About the Venture<br></strong></p><p>We are building AI infrastructure. Our pre-seed funding is secured, there is early customer demand and the product is already in production.</p><p>We are now looking for a Lead Engineer to build the core of the product with us, set the technical direction and grow the engineering team.<br></p><p><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p>As Lead Engineer, you will spend most of your time building. At least 80% of your week is hands-on coding on our core systems. The rest goes into setting the technical direction, leading a team of 2 engineers and helping us hire as the team grows.</p><p>We are an AI-native engineering team, with agentic engineering at the centre of how we write, review and ship code. Coding agents such as Claude Code are the default way we build software, not an add-on.</p><p>We are at a very early stage. Many of the important technical decisions are still ahead, and you will be one of the people making them.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul><li><p>Write code every day and contribute directly to our core systems, from APIs to cloud infrastructure</p></li><li><p>Set the technical direction with the founding team, from architecture to build-vs-buy decisions</p></li><li><p>Lead and support our team of 2 engineers, review their work and set high engineering standards</p></li><li><p>Support technical hiring and help shape how the engineering team grows</p></li><li><p>Build and improve our agentic engineering setup, from harnesses and workflows to running multiple agents in parallel, evaluating their output and benchmarking what works</p></li><li><p>Build and operate reliable AI infrastructure, with security, GDPR and European data residency built in</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><p><strong>About You</strong></p><p>You are a strong engineer who loves to build and is interested in more than the code itself. You care about how a team works, how technical decisions get made and how an engineering organisation takes shape at an early stage. You may already have led a team, or you may be a senior engineer ready to step into a lead role and take on the responsibility that comes with it.</p><ul><li><p>Strong backend and platform foundations, including distributed systems, API design, cloud infrastructure and production systems</p></li><li><p>Hands-on experience building LLM-powered systems or AI infrastructure in production</p></li><li><p>Extensive daily use of coding agents such as Claude Code, with strong coding fundamentals and the judgement to review and own the quality of their output</p></li><li><p>Experience designing and improving agentic engineering workflows, including harnesses, multi-agent orchestration and benchmarking, with a clear understanding of where agents help and where they fall short</p></li><li><p>Experience as a Lead Engineer or Tech Lead, ideally in an early-stage startup, or as a senior engineer who has mentored others and is ready to step into a lead role</p></li><li><p>A real interest in more than coding, including setting the technical direction, leading a team and hiring</p></li><li><p>Fluent English; German is a plus<br></p></li></ul><p><strong>Why Join</strong></p><p>Funding is secured and the product is already in production, but most of the important technical decisions are still ahead. You will write a lot of code, shape the architecture and help build the team from the start, with equity in the business you help build.<br></p><p><strong>This is a full-time role, based in our Berlin office 5 days a week, starting as soon as possible.</strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p> <br> <p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/atlanticvc/lead-engineer-gn-at-ai-venture-berlin-78333","tags":["Portfolio Company"],"job_types":["Experienced","fulltime permanent"],"location":"Berlin, Berlin, Germany","created_at":1793935909},{"slug":"senior-field-operations-manager-koln-211152","company_name":"Fastned","title":"Senior Field Operations Manager","description":"<p style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">Fastned is one of Europe's leading fast-charging networks. Active across nine countries, we have spent nearly 15 years building the infrastructure, expertise and brand that define premium fast charging in Europe. What sets us apart is our focus on reliability, sustainability and the energy transition. We have been awarded “Best Charging Network” in the UK, France, Switzerland and the Netherlands, further establishing Fastned as a leading player in the field. This is your opportunity to make a lasting impact and help us accelerate our operations in the DACH region to the next level! Join Fastned at the forefront of Europe’s electric vehicle and charging infrastructure revolution.</span></strong></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><strong><span style="color:#000000">The role is based in our beautiful office in Cologne, where your over 50 future colleagues cannot wait to meet you!</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#000000">Your role</span></strong></h3><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">As Senior Operations Manager DACH, you will initially focus on Germany and Switzerland while helping shape the future of operations across the wider DACH region, including Austria as the organisation expands. Germany is entering a major growth phase, with the network expected to expand significantly in the coming years. You will help design an operating model that can absorb this growth while keeping uptime above 99%, improving customer experience and managing costs and team growth responsibly.</span></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">You will have significant ownership of how operations are run in Germany and Switzerland. As the key operational point of contact for German, Swiss and future Austrian stations, you will work closely with country and central teams, as well as contractors and service providers. Your scope spans preventive maintenance of chargers and stations, station appearance and amenities, reactive maintenance, spare parts logistics, and the continuous improvement of our operations and processes. Within the broader direction set by Fastned, you will define priorities, improve the operating model and make pragmatic decisions that keep the region performing as the network grows.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#000000">Your responsibilities</span></strong></h3><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Team leadership</span></strong></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Lead and grow the DACH field team.</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Supervising, coaching and developing a team of five Field Engineers and a Station Manager, with a Maintenance Coordinator joining over time, ensuring they work safely, efficiently and as one strong team.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Managing team capacity, prioritising work and dispatching jobs in the most efficient way across the Swiss and German network.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Bringing structure to the team’s priorities and ways of working, helping ensure maintenance work is completed on time and the network remains safe, reliable and available for our customers.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Creating a strong safety culture by ensuring full compliance with Health &amp; Safety standards and regulatory requirements, and providing a safe and caring work environment for colleagues on the road and on site.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Operational excellence</span></strong></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">Ensure high uptime and a great station experience.</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Being accountable for all day-to-day operations of Fastned stations in the DACH region, from chargers and systems to the overall look and feel of our sites.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Ensuring we maintain network uptime above 99% in your region through effective preventive maintenance plans and swift, high-quality reactive repairs.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Managing a network of partners responsible for maintaining and servicing our stations.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Supporting improvements to the customer experience and your team in the field by regularly visiting stations, performing site inspections and quality audits, with a strong focus on safety and customer experience.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Overseeing the handover of new stations in the DACH region from Construction to Field Operations, ensuring they meet our operational, safety and quality standards from day one.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Managing spare parts flows together with our Supply Chain team to optimise local stock levels, minimise downtime and ensure that engineers always have the right parts at the right time.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Leading and coordinating with external partners larger infrastructure works at your stations.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Continuously improving how we work by taking local initiatives, standardising best practices, simplifying processes and using data and insights to make better decisions.</span></p></li></ul><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Customer, stakeholder and partner management</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Delivering a best-in-class customer experience by ensuring stations are always clean, safe and easy to use, with strong attention to detail across lighting, signage, landscaping, cleanliness and amenities.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Collaborating closely with Customer Operations and other internal teams to monitor performance, respond to incidents and ensure a smooth, end-to-end customer journey across the network.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Acting as the voice of DACH Operations within the leadership team and central organisations, representing operational priorities and insights.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Initiating, developing and maintaining strong relationships with external partners and contractors, such as electrical contractors, cleaning, landscaping and civil works providers. Providing operational input into new station designs, upgrades and local initiatives to ensure operational excellence is embedded from the outset.</span></p></li></ul><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">You will report to our Director of Operations, based in Amsterdam. The role is based in Germany and involves regular travel across the DACH region to visit stations and team members, as well as occasional travel to our Amsterdam headquarters.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#000000">Who are we looking for?</span></strong></h3><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">You are a seasoned field operations leader who can both set direction and get things done on the ground. You combine a strategic mindset with strong operational experience, and you are excited to scale and professionalise Fastned’s German and Swiss operations. You think in terms of network performance, customer experience and long-term capabilities, while also being comfortable jumping into the details when needed to remove blockers for your team.</span></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">In addition, you meet most of the following criteria:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You have at least eight years of relevant experience in operations roles.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You have proven experience scaling or professionalising operations in a growing market, for example by building teams, introducing new ways of working, improving performance and enhancing customer experience.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You are a strong people leader who coaches and develops your team, communicates clearly and stands your ground when needed, leads by example in the field, and creates a safe, high-performance culture.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You combine a strategic mindset, including the ability to set a vision for DACH Operations, define priorities and align stakeholders, with hands-on senior operational experience. You are comfortable going on site, understanding technical issues and making pragmatic trade-offs.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You remain calm and organised under pressure, can manage multiple priorities at once and maintain a positive, can-do attitude.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You are a strong communicator and stakeholder manager, able to connect the needs of the German and Swiss operations with those of our central teams and influence decisions where needed.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">You are fluent in English and German. Any additional European language is a plus.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p></li></ul><h3><strong><span style="color:#000000">Join us in building a better future</span></strong></h3><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">We work hard to change the world, but we do not forget to recognise and celebrate our successes, big and small. We value work-life balance, offer real work flexibility and have family-friendly policies in place. We have an inclusive work environment and love authentic people, so do not try to fit in because we like you for who you are!</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A fully electric company car, with all charging expenses covered.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">29 days of annual leave.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Two Mission Days each year to support a cause you care about or contribute to our mission.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A company bonus plan that recognises the impact you make.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A Deutschlandticket covered by Fastned.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">An annual personal development budget of €3,000, because there is always more to learn and improve.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Mental wellbeing support through nilo health.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A subsidised Urban Sports Club membership.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Access to women’s health experts through our partnership with Flouria.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">A laptop and phone of your choice, with an EU-wide mobile phone plan.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Daily vegetarian lunches, snacks and drinks at our office locations.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Team events throughout the year, an annual company trip and our legendary Christmas parties.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h3><strong><span style="color:#000000">Interested? Apply today!</span></strong></h3><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">We would love to have a conversation with you! Apply now, send us your CV and explain in your cover letter why you are excited about joining our mission for freedom in sustainable transportation.</span></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><span style="color:#000000">We are looking forward to your application!</span></p><p><br></p><p style="text-align:justify;"><em><span style="color:#000000">Fastned stands for equity and inclusion. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds, gender identities, sexual orientations, religions, neurodiversity, disabilities, parental status or any other protected characteristic that makes you unique</span></em></p><p>