&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently identify/design analytic tasks and contribute to the development of overall analytic framework for consulting projects;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with client representatives to communicate developments and present results;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft reports or presentations, or sections of reports or presentations;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to project planning and budget management efforts;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide training and technical supervision to less-experienced staff, including reviewing their analyses and providing coaching/direction;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to business development efforts and draft client proposals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in life sciences (e.g., biology, biotechnology, biochemistry, pharmacology, chemistry etc.) or a relevant analytical degree, with significant work experience;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-6 years previous consulting experience;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong skills in quantitative and qualitative analysis methods and techniques;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven staff and project management skills;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Client interaction, facilitation, presentation, budgeting, and project planning skills;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of pricing and market access issues in the European markets (and globally);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasional travel required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To Apply&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To be considered for this position, we require the following:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resume&lt;/strong&gt; – please include current address, personal email and telephone number;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cover letter&lt;/strong&gt; – please describe your interest in CRA and how this role matches your goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Career Growth and Benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CRA’s robust &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.crai.com/cra-careers/talent-development/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;skills development programs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, including a commitment to offering training annually through formal and informal programs, encouraging you to thrive as an individual and team member. Beginning with skill building, training continues with technical training, presentation skills, internal seminars, and career mentoring and performance coaching from an assigned senior colleague. Additional leadership and collaboration opportunities exist through internal firm development activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We offer a comprehensive total rewards program including a superior benefits package, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.crai.com/benefits/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;wellness programmin&lt;/strong&gt;g&lt;/a&gt; to support physical, mental, emotional and financial well-being, and in-house &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.crai.com/cra-careers/immigration-global-mobility/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;immigration support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; for foreign nationals and international business travelers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location Flexibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CRA creates a work environment that enables our colleagues to benefit from being together in the office to best deliver on our promise of career growth, mentorship and inclusivity. At the same time, we recognise that individuals realise a range of benefits when working from home periodically. We currently expect that individuals spend at least 3 to 4 days a week working in the office (which may include traveling to another CRA office or to client meetings), with specific days determined in coordination with your practice or team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsible AI Use in Recruiting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that recruiting is fundamentally a human process, and we are committed to a hiring process that is consistent, transparent, and people-focused. While AI and other technology-enabled tools help our team operate more efficiently, we strive to provide every candidate with a personalized, thoughtful, and high-touch experience. As CRA invests significant human effort to find qualified members for our teams, we expect candidates to invest corresponding human effort to learn about CRA, prepare thoughtful application materials, and engage with our interviewers. Read more about appropriate hiring manager, recruiting team, and candidate AI at CRA &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.crai.com/cra-careers/ai-recruiting/&quot;&gt;on our website&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Equal Employment Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Charles River Associates is an equal opportunity employer (Equality Act 2010). All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other protected characteristic under applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;____________________________________________________________________________________________________________________&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Über Charles River Associates&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Charles River Associates&lt;/strong&gt; ist eine führende globale Beratungsfirma, die wirtschaftliche, finanzielle und betriebswirtschaftliche Expertise für große Anwaltskanzleien, Unternehmen und Regierungen weltweit bietet. CRA berät Kunden in wirtschaftlichen und finanziellen Angelegenheiten im Zusammenhang mit Rechtsstreitigkeiten und behördlichen Verfahren und unterstützt Unternehmen bei kritischen Geschäftsstrategien und leistungsbezogenen Fragen. Seit 1965 engagieren Kunden CRA aufgrund der Kombination aus Branchenerfahrung und rigoroser, faktenbasierter Analyse, die klare, umsetzbare Lösungen für komplexe Geschäftsprobleme bietet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stellenübersicht&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Die Life Sciences Practice von CRA hilft Pharma-, Biotechnologie-, Medtech- und Digital-Health-Unternehmen, optimale Leistungen in wichtigen Geschäftsbereichen wie kommerzielle Strategie, Preisgestaltung und Zugang, Innovation, Organisationsstruktur, Politikanalyse, medizinische Angelegenheiten, Stakeholder-Management und Marketing zu erzielen – alles zum langfristigen Nutzen von Patienten, Ärzten, Mitarbeitern und Aktionären. Wir arbeiten direkt mit Life-Sciences-Unternehmen sowie mit deren Rechtsberatern, Industrieverbänden, Regierungsorganisationen und Interessengruppen zusammen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Associate Principals bei CRA arbeiten gemeinsam mit erfahrenen und jüngeren Consultants in Projektteams an einer Vielzahl von Kundenprojekten in unterschiedlichen Branchen. Sie führen anspruchsvolle strategische Analysen durch und unterstützen bei der Steuerung von Beratungsprojekten. Dabei übernehmen sie die Projektleitung, koordinieren die Arbeit anderer Teammitglieder, verantworten Analysen, betreuen Kundenbeziehungen auf mittlerer Ebene und/oder kommunizieren Projektergebnisse. In dieser Position arbeiten Sie weitgehend selbstständig und eigenverantwortlich.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Für eine erfolgreiche Tätigkeit in dieser Position sollten Sie in der Lage sein, kleinere Projekte oder wesentliche Teilaufgaben größerer und komplexerer Projekte effektiv zu planen und zu steuern, Fragestellungen zu strukturieren und zu analysieren sowie ein breites Spektrum analytischer Aufgaben selbst durchzuführen oder anzuleiten. Darüber hinaus legen wir großen Wert auf eine ausgeprägte Arbeitsethik, Kreativität, eine positive Einstellung und ein hohes Maß an Engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Aktuell suchen wir insbesondere Consultants mit fundierten Kenntnissen der Pricing- und Market-Access-Systeme in Europa und weltweit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Aufgaben&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie identifizieren und konzipieren eigenständig die erforderlichen Analysen und wirken an der Entwicklung des übergreifenden analytischen Ansatzes für Beratungsprojekte mit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie stehen im direkten Austausch mit unseren Kunden, informieren sie über den Projektfortschritt und präsentieren Ergebnisse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie erstellen Berichte und Präsentationen oder übernehmen die Ausarbeitung einzelner Abschnitte.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie wirken bei der Projektplanung und der Steuerung von Projektbudgets mit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie unterstützen weniger erfahrene Teammitglieder bei ihrer fachlichen Weiterentwicklung, prüfen deren Analysen und geben ihnen fachliche Anleitung und Feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sie bringen sich in die Geschäftsentwicklung ein und wirken bei der Erstellung von Angeboten für Kunden mit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gewünschte Qualifikationen&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor- oder Masterabschluss im Bereich Life Sciences, z. B. in Biologie, Biotechnologie, Biochemie, Pharmakologie oder Chemie, oder in einem relevanten Studiengang mit analytischem Schwerpunkt sowie einschlägige Berufserfahrung;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 bis 7 Jahre Berufserfahrung in der Beratung;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fundierte Kenntnisse und Erfahrung in der Anwendung quantitativer und qualitativer Analysemethoden;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nachweisliche Erfahrung in der Mitarbeiterführung und im Projektmanagement;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Erfahrung im direkten Kundenkontakt, in der Moderation und Präsentation sowie in der Budget- und Projektplanung;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fundierte Kenntnisse zu Pricing und Market Access in europäischen und internationalen Märkten;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deutschkenntnisse von Vorteil;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bereitschaft zu gelegentlichen Dienstreisen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bewerbung&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Um für diese Position berücksichtigt zu werden, reichen Sie bitte die folgenden Unterlagen ein:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lebenslauf&lt;/strong&gt; – bitte geben Sie Ihre aktuelle Adresse, eprsönliche E-Mail-Adresse und Telefonnummer an;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anschreiben&lt;/strong&gt; – Bitte beschreiben Sie Ihr Interesse an CRA und wie diese Rolle zu Ihren Zielen passt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Karriereentwicklung und Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CRA bietet Ihnen vielfältige Möglichkeiten zur fachlichen und persönlichen Weiterentwicklung. Dazu gehören jährliche formelle und informelle Weiterbildungsangebote, die Ihre individuelle Entwicklung ebenso fördern wie Ihre Zusammenarbeit im Team. Das Angebot reicht von Trainings zur Weiterentwicklung Ihrer fachlichen und persönlichen Kompetenzen über Präsentationstrainings und interne Seminare bis hin zu individuellem Karriere-Mentoring und Performance-Coaching durch eine erfahrene Kollegin oder einen erfahrenen Kollegen. Darüber hinaus bieten interne Initiativen die Möglichkeit, zusätzliche Führungsverantwortung zu übernehmen und sich aktiv in die Weiterentwicklung von CRA einzubringen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wir bieten Ihnen ein umfassendes Vergütungs- und Leistungspaket mit attraktiven Zusatzleistungen. Dazu gehören Angebote zur Förderung Ihres körperlichen, mentalen, emotionalen und finanziellen Wohlbefindens sowie interne Unterstützung bei Einwanderungs- und Visaangelegenheiten für internationale Mitarbeitende und Geschäftsreisende.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexibilität am Arbeitsplatz&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CRA schafft ein Arbeitsumfeld, das es unseren Kollegen ermöglicht, von der Zusammenarbeit im Büro zu profitieren, um unser Versprechen von beruflichem Wachstum, Mentoring und Inklusivität bestmöglich zu erfüllen. Gleichzeitig erkennen wir an, dass Einzelpersonen eine Reihe von Vorteilen genießen, wenn sie periodisch von zu Hause aus arbeiten. Derzeit bitten wir Mitarbeiter, im Durchschnitt 3 bis 4 Tage die Woche im Büro zu arbeiten (was Reisen zu einem anderen CRA-Büro oder zum Standort eines Kunden einschließen kann). Zu bestimmten Zeiten des Jahres (z.B. Feiertagsperioden) werden zusätzliche Remote-Arbeitsoptionen für diejenigen angeboten, deren Arbeitsverpflichtungen dies zulassen, obwohl unsere Büros für diejenigen, die dort sein möchten oder müssen, geöffnet bleiben.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unser Engagement für Vielfalt&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Charles River Associates ist ein Arbeitgeber, der Chancengleichheit bietet. Im Rahmen unseres Fokus auf Gerechtigkeit und Inklusion arbeiten wir daran, einen fairen und konsistenten Einstellungsprozess sicherzustellen. Wir feiern Vielfalt und sind für ein inklusives Arbeitsumfeld engagiert.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/charlesriverassociates/associate-principal-pricing-market-access-life-sciences-practice-munich-498390","tags":["Life Sciences"],"job_types":[],"location":"Munich","created_at":1793926522},{"slug":"ai-data-analytics-partner-germany-96964","company_name":"Jimdo","title":"AI & Data Analytics Partner","description":"<h2><strong>About Jimdo<br /></strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We exist to unleash the power of the self-employed - helping solopreneurs and micro-businesses thrive by doing what they're passionate about and removing the complexity of building lasting, successful businesses.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Jimdo started in 2007 when three school friends built a website builder in a Northern German farmhouse to help everyone build a presence online. Today, we're a profitable, remote-first company with 220+ people from 50+ nationalities working across 15+ countries. We've helped build over 36 million websites to get online across the world.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're more than just a website builder. We're an AI-powered platform that helps self-employed people actually run and build successful businesses — from getting found online, winning customers and running their business with a peace of mind by knowing exactly what to do next to move forward.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At the heart of Jimdo is a strong belief in personalized, data-driven guidance. Our platform combines design, business tools, and an AI-powered core that turns real customer data into clear insights and next steps helping our customers focus on what moves their business forward.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Role Overview:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Jimdo is becoming an AI-first company, and our People team is one of the first places where that shows up in daily work. We're looking for an AI &amp; Data Analytics Partner to build the agents, analytics and workflow automations that make the People team faster, smarter and easier to scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll take a process from "this is slow and manual" to a working, compliant solution in production, and then make sure the team can run and extend it without you. You'll also give leadership one reliable view of People data, so decisions rest on numbers everyone trusts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll start with the People team, and the scope can grow to any other function across Jimdo.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The team and who you'll work with:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll report to the Manager Performance Intelligence and work day to day with the People team and our HR Business Partners.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll also work closely with our AI team on standards and capabilities, with Finance and Legal on data consistency and compliance, and with our HR system and payroll providers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a remote role, open to candidates based in Germany, Italy, Spain or Portugal.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll be doing:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a central reporting suite in Tableau that brings data from HiBob, payroll and compensation tools into one source of truth, with dashboards leadership actually uses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the quality and structure of People data, and use analytics to spot workforce trends, risks and process bottlenecks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find the HR processes with the most friction and fix them with AI agents and workflow automation, from first prototype to production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve self-service for employees and managers with AI tools that answer the repetitive questions, so the People team can focus on the work that needs a person.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Connect our systems of record and improve the data flow between HR and Finance, so there's far less manual reconciliation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make every solution auditable, explainable and compliant, and set clear guardrails for responsible AI use.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run hands-on workshops and co-building sessions and write playbooks, so the team can build and maintain automations on their own.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Your first months:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">After 3 months: you know our People systems and data flows, you've agreed the reporting scope with the People team, and your first quick-win automation is live.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">After 6 months: the central reporting suite is in use by leadership, and at least one AI-enabled HR process runs in production</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you bring to the table:</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in data analytics, AI and automation, or technical systems roles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2+ years of hands-on work with LLMs, agents, prompt engineering and workflow orchestration tools such as n8n, with solutions you've taken into production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of improving business processes through automation or system redesign, with results you can show.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong data analysis skills and expert-level Tableau: you build dashboards that turn complex data into clear recommendations. Database knowledge is a plus.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expert knowledge of HiBob as a user, including its data and reporting, and a solid sense of data privacy and compliance (GDPR) when handling sensitive people data.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You enjoy teaching: you explain technical choices in plain language and measure your success by how well others can use what you've built.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Nice to have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct experience in an HR or People Operations team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A certification in AI, machine learning, analytics or automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with Finance, Legal or external HR service providers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What we offer:<br /></strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>Inspiring Mission:</u></strong> At our core, we are driven by a meaningful mission - to  empower solopreneurs and small businesses to succeed and  to contribute to the sustainability and vibrancy of the communities they serve.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>Flexibility and Trust:</u></strong> Our work environment thrives on flexibility and trust. We offer fully remote work set-up  with opportunities for in-person collaboration. You can manage your working hours flexibly because we prioritize the results you deliver over the number of hours you put in. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>An International Diverse Team:</u></strong> Our team is a mosaic of over 248 individuals hailing from 50+ different countries and working across 15+ diverse locations. We take pride in our openness and inclusivity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>Continuous  Growth and Career Development:</u></strong> We invest in your growth with company-wide access to LinkedIn Learning and curated learning paths. From day one, you have the chance to contribute your ideas and create a meaningful impact. Our flat hierarchies and swift decision-making processes provide an open platform for your career progression.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><u>Competitive Benefits Package: </u></strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Annual compensation reviews to ensure you're rewarded fairly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A remote office set-up bonus to enhance your workspace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An employee assistance program, offering resources and counseling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plus, a perk that keeps giving: up to three free Jimdo websites for your personal or professional projects that you get to keep forever.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Jimdo is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. This means that we don’t discriminate based on race or ethnic origin, color, the language(s) you speak, where you (or your parents) are from, or whether or not you consider yourself to have a disability. Neither will your age, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, beliefs, or political opinions play a part in your application with us. Our diverse team values and celebrates the uniqueness of each individual. We embrace differences and believe that they enrich our organization, making us stronger and more innovative. Join us, and let's continue to create a workplace where everyone can thrive, regardless of background or identity.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><br />By sending your application, you declare that you read and understand the </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.jimdo.com/info/privacy-applicants/?_ncr=true"><em>Jimdo Applicant Privacy Policy</em></a></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/jimdo/ai-data-analytics-partner-germany-96964","tags":["Data & Analytics"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Germany","created_at":1793925614},{"slug":"staff-robotic-sales-engineer-munich-276910","company_name":"RobCo","title":"Staff Robotic Sales Engineer (m/f/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role at RobCo</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">RobCo is building the category of Autonomous Industrial Robotics and we're doing it fast. We believe that automating the ordinary frees humans to do the extraordinary, and we're building the end-to-end robotics infrastructure to make that possible - hardware, software, and AI in one stack that just works. </p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our Staff Robotic Sales Engineer (m/f/d), you are RobCo's most senior technical voice in sales, owning your own deals alongside Account Executives while setting the technical standards that make the whole Robotics Sales Engineering team stronger. If something is broken, you fix it. If something can be automated, you build it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a technical leadership role without people management. You keep a quota with your own Account Executives, and a fixed part of your time goes into raising the technical bar across the team. You work where modular robotics, software and AI come together, and you help bring physical AI from the lab into real production. Sales leadership turns to you first when they want to know how strong the pipeline really is.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define how the team judges feasibility, including real-world limits beyond data sheets, edge cases and clear no-go criteria</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop our requirement workshop format and handover standards further</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Step into complex or escalating deals across the team, set the technical direction and stay involved until the responsible RSE can carry the case forward</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make the go/no-go call on difficult feasibility cases, review concepts before handover and approve larger price indications</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build reusable assets such as calculation models, reference layouts per use case and enablement material for Sales and our partners</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track which use cases keep coming up and which we win or lose, and feed these insights into focus areas and the product roadmap</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape onboarding and ramp-up for new RSEs and give technical feedback across the team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pitch to strategic customers, give talks at trade fairs and events, and decide with Marketing and Product what we demo and why</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay the technical lead for your own Account Executives and share their quota</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We're looking for someone who has:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extensive experience in technical pre-sales, application engineering or automation projects, including time at a senior level</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working against a quota and winning complex deals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record as the person colleagues turn to when a feasibility question gets hard</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to recognize patterns across projects and turn them into rules, templates and tools that others use</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading through expertise, with the trust of engineers and sales leaders in your technical judgement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The confidence to make a go/no-go call and stand behind it, even when a deal is on t