rk closely with senior client stakeholders, sales teams, and technical specialists to shape digital commerce solutions, lead discovery workshops, and support new business opportunities.</p><p>The ideal candidate understands how different e-commerce platforms and customer-facing technologies work together, can advise clients on the right solutions, and is comfortable collaborating with commercial teams.</p><h3>Key Responsibilities</h3><ul><li>Advise Retail &amp; CPG clients on e-commerce, digital customer experience, personalization, customer data and technology transformation.</li><li>Translate business requirements into solution concepts, capability roadmaps and target architectures.</li><li>Lead discovery sessions and solution design workshops with business and IT stakeholders.</li><li>Advise on the integration of commerce platforms, CDPs, marketing technologies, PIM, OMS and other digital commerce systems.</li><li>Collaborate with sales and pre-sales teams to identify client opportunities, develop proposals and shape consulting engagements.</li><li>Stay informed about DACH retail trends, marketplace dynamics, emerging technologies and changing customer expectations.</li><li>Develop reusable consulting assets, including reference architectures, solution frameworks, demonstrations and go-to-market offerings.</li><li>Build relationships with senior decision-makers, including CDOs, CMOs, CIOs, and Heads of E-commerce.</li><li>Collaborate with regional and global technology teams to support the growth of the Retail &amp; CPG practice.</li><li>Represent the company at client meetings, industry conferences, and relevant networking events.</li></ul><h3>Key Areas of Expertise</h3><p>We are particularly interested in candidates who understand the broader digital commerce ecosystem and how its different technologies connect.</p><p>Relevant areas include:</p><ul><li><strong>E-commerce platforms:</strong> commercetools, Salesforce Commerce Cloud, SAP Commerce, Adobe Commerce, Shopify Plus, headless and composable commerce.</li><li><strong>Customer data and CDPs:</strong> Salesforce Data Cloud, Adobe Real-Time CDP, Segment, mParticle, Tealium, Bloomreach, first-party data and consent management.</li><li><strong>Marketing technology and personalization:</strong> Braze, Salesforce Marketing Cloud, Klaviyo, Emarsys, Dynamic Yield, Algolia, Optimizely and customer journey optimization.</li><li><strong>Commerce architecture and integrations:</strong> OMS, PIM, DAM, APIs, system integrations, distributed order management and omnichannel fulfillment.</li><li><strong>Marketplaces and retail media:</strong> Amazon, Zalando, Otto, Kaufland, retail media networks, marketplace integrations and D2C business models.</li><li><strong>Emerging commerce technologies:</strong> AI-assisted shopping, conversational commerce, GenAI applications, loyalty solutions and digital customer engagement.</li></ul><p>Expertise across every platform is not required. What matters most is understanding how these technologies work together and recommending solutions that match clients' business needs.</p><h3>Your Profile</h3><ul><li><strong>At least 5 years of relevant experience in e-commerce or digital commerce</strong>, ideally within Retail &amp; CPG.</li><li>Background in IT consulting, digital transformation, systems integration, technology services, or digital commerce consulting.</li><li>Technical-functional understanding of e-commerce platforms, system integrations, data flows, and digital customer-facing solutions.</li><li>Experience working directly with clients, gathering requirements, leading workshops, and developing solution recommendations.</li><li>Familiarity with pre-sales processes and the ability to collaborate effectively with sales teams.</li><li>Understanding of the DACH retail and CPG market, including major retailers, marketplace dynamics, digital commerce trends, and GDPR requirements.</li><li>Ability to communicate complex technology concepts to 