<li>Own features end to end, from shaping the product spec through technical design, implementation, testing, deployment, and production monitoring. You won’t just receive work from product: as a domain expert, you’ll help define what we build and propose the work you consider most useful</li>
<li>Integrate with external partners such as banks, payment processors, blockchains, and identity and compliance vendors, and build the abstractions that make those integrations reliable</li>
<li>Improve engineering quality across observability, incident response, security practices, and API design</li>
<li>Collaborate closely with product, compliance, and other engineering teams across MoonPay’s global network</li>
<li>(Staff level) Set technical direction for your area, mentor other engineers, and drive architectural decisions that span multiple teams</li>
</ul>
<h2>About you</h2>
<ul style="list-style-type: disc;">
<li>5+ years of backend engineering experience (8+ for Staff), with a track record of shipping and operating production systems at scale</li>
<li>Strong backend experience with a statically compiled language (e.g. Rust, Go, C#, C++) is a must. Deep fundamentals matter more to us than your specific language history</li>
<li>Prior professional Rust experience is not required, but interest in Rust and motivation to become an expert in it are very welcome, since our services are written in Rust</li>
<li>Solid fundamentals in distributed systems, API design, data modeling, and asynchronous processing</li>
<li>Comfort working in domains where precision matters, such as financial systems, double-entry ledgers, reconciliation, or similarly correctness-critical software</li>
<li>A pragmatic, autonomous, ownership-driven mindset. You care about outcomes, communicate clearly, and thrive on high throughput: on this team, features ship in hours to days and products in days to weeks</li>
<li>Strong critical thinking, including in how you use AI tools. You know how to drive AI-assisted development productively while staying firmly in control of correctness, security, and design quality</li>
<li>Interest in crypto, stablecoins, and the future of payments. Prior crypto experience is a plus rather than a requirement, except for Track 3, where hands-on blockchain development experience is expected</li>
</ul>
<h2>Bonus points</h2>
<ul style="list-style-type: disc;">
<li>Professional or hobby experience writing Rust (open-source contributions count!)</li>
<li>Experience in fiat payments, banking integrations, card networks, or PSPs</li>
