em">Doit is building its investment business from Vilnius. As Compliance Director and AML at Doit Lithuania, you will build and run our compliance and anti-money-laundering function from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will act as our Compliance Officer and AML Officer, and report directly to the management board. You will be independent of the business lines you monitor. You will run compliance and AML for a digital investment platform serving clients in Lithuania and across the European Economic Area.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Own</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and own the compliance and AML/CTF policies and procedures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the business-wide AML risk assessment, customer risk scoring and risk appetite.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design remote onboarding controls with our KYC partners, including enhanced due diligence for PEPs and high-risk clients.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and tune transaction monitoring scenarios for brokerage activity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run sanctions screening at onboarding, on an ongoing basis and on payments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">File suspicious activity reports with the FNTT and suspicious order reports under MAR.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the compliance monitoring programme and report to the board.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Approve marketing communications and oversee product governance, complaints and conflicts of interest.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the regulatory relationship with the Bank of Lithuania on compliance and AML matters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare the firm for the EU AML Regulation, which applies from July 2027.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the compliance and AML team as the business grows.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant experience in AML/CTF at a regulated EU financial institution. Ideally at an investment firm, neobroker, neobank or e-money institution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with digital onboarding and remote identity verification at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience building risk assessments, monitoring scenarios and EDD processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience filing suspicious activity reports and handling regulatory inspections.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of MiFID II conduct and investment-services compliance, or the ability to learn it fast.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience selecting and overseeing KYC, screening and monitoring tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong judgment and the confidence to challenge senior colleagues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear, concise writing for policies, board reports and regulators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clean record and good reputation, suitable for regulatory approval as a key function holder.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Based in Lithuania, or open to relocating to Lithuania.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to Have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lithuanian language ability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An existing working relationship with the Bank of Lithuania or the FNTT.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of Lithuanian AML law and Bank of Lithuania instructions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with clients across several EEA countries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CAMS (ACAMS) or ICA certification.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"