cing law and their legal mindset to ask thoughtful questions to understand the needs of law firm and in-house attorneys, develop credibility, and then partner with Account Executives to educate them on Harvey’s value via large and small group sessions as well as one-to-one conversations.</p><h1></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead, coach, and develop a team of Legal Engineers, setting clear performance expectations and building a high-trust, high-output team culture</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the quality and consistency of Harvey's pre-sales legal engineering function, ensuring demos, discovery conversations, and deal support are delivered to the highest standard</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with Account Executives and GTM leadership to prioritise pipeline, develop deal strategy, and support conversion on complex or strategic opportunities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engage with lawyers at prospective customers to understand and address their workflow challenges</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with Product and Marketing to ensure the team's field insights are feeding into positioning, roadmap, and go-to-market strategy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead product demonstrations tailored to the context of various law firm practice groups and in-house legal teams, asking questions to validate how Harvey can add value and then showcasing Harvey’s features and benefits relevant to each prospective client’s potential use cases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the “Voice of the Customer,” using your legal perspective to help the broader sales team to develop and implement more effective strategies and synthesize customer feedback for the product team through a legal lens.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Travel may be required from time to time, including visits t