ost companies don't have time for, all while having fun and never taking ourselves too seriously.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've raised $100+ million from Index Ventures, Insight Partners, and Point Nine, and we're growing fast. There's never been a better time to join.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring a Product Ops Associate to work closely with our Product Management team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is about is about giving leverage to our product leaders. You’ll pick up a mix of strategic and hands-on work — sometimes shaping big decisions, other times rolling up your sleeves to get the basics right. Both matter. You might be driving projects like pushing through legal and financial documentation to get local branches set up across the world or ensuring that GTM is getting all relevant customer feedback back to Product. The common thread: it's important, and it needs doing well.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be dropped into unfamiliar situations. You’ll need to learn quickly, and be trusted to make good calls. You’ll need to be comfortable with ambiguity, happy to work things out from first principles, and confident context switching often. The work is not always glamorous (not much of startup work is!), but it’s always meaningful.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s a great fit for someone who’s curious, quick, and thrives in ambiguity. You’ll get a front-row seat to how we build and scale products — ideal if you want to continue within an operations-esque role or continue to work within some related product role. It’s also great if you want exposure to the scale-up world before choosing where to specialise.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What that looks like day to day</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Acting as a right hand to our Product Managers: someone who can be trusted to just figure it out</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">While you will be working in Product, you’ll be expected to build relationships and get stuff done with leaders across all functions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Breaking down big, messy problems into actionable steps and delivering results</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Switching between projects (like figuring out how to extend the reach and stability of our telecom operations) and hands-on work (like supporting our Salesforce application process)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spotting inefficiencies or gaps and putting systems in place to fix them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Doing the unglamorous work when it matters because sometimes, that’s what’s needed</p></li></ul><h2>Who you are</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a fast-paced environment (e.g. startup, consulting, banking, founding experience)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High ownership and bias to action above all else, you get things done</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fast learner with strong analytical thinking</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident communicator who works well across functions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with ambiguity, and quick to bring clarity</p></li></ul><h2>Supporting you</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work hard and we think life outside work matters just as much. Our benefits pack is built to support both.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Private medical insurance.</strong> Seriously good cover - we want you and the people you love to be looked after.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive annual leave.</strong> Showing up at your best requires switching off, and we make sure you have time to do that.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First Friday of every month off.</strong> Yes, seriously.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enhanced pension.</strong> We put real money in, because future-you deserves better than an afterthought.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meaningful equity.</strong> We're rapidly scaling, and everyone who helps shape the outcome should share in it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unlimited AI spend.</strong> For everyone, not just engineers. We're all-in on AI across the company, and we expect you to be too.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Generous parental leave.</strong> The early days with a new baby matter more than anything we're doing here, and we want you to be present for them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Two budgets that have your back.</strong> £1000 to invest in your setup, £500 a year to invest in yourself.</p></li></ul><hr><p>Compensation: £55K – £75.5K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • £55K – £75.5K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/incidentio/product-operations-associate-london-493911","tags":["Product Development"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793958015},{"slug":"business-development-representative-london-470568","company_name":"incident.io","title":"Business Development Representative","description":"<h1>A little about us</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://incident.io">incident.io</a> is the AI software reliability platform trusted by engineering teams at Notion, Linear, Ramp and 2,000+ companies who can't afford downtime.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The stakes are real, the talent is insane, and somehow it's a genuinely lovely place to work. We all pull our weight, go the extra mile, and put in the bit of magic most companies don't have time for, all while having fun and never taking ourselves too seriously.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've raised $100+ million from Index Ventures, Insight Partners, and Point Nine, and we're growing fast. There's never been a better time to join.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The role in one line</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Being a BDR at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://incident.io">incident.io</a> means learning to sell from some of the best in the business, while representing a product and account team that make every conversation an easy one to be proud of.</p><h2><strong>What that looks like day to day</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cold calling is the heart of this role, and most of our meetings get booked over the phone - not because it's easy, but because it's still the fastest way to build real trust with a prospect. We don't copy-paste templates, and we don't spam: every call and every piece of outreach is backed by careful research and planning alongside the AEs you partner with, so the person on the other end knows you're not a random dial.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're founded by engineers, and that shows up in how BDRs work too, everyone gets unlimited Claude tokens, and our head of business development is a former RevOps leader himself, so there's a real emphasis on testing, measuring, and optimizing your own workflow like an engineer would, not just running the same script on repeat.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BDRs are the bench for our wider GTM team, and your progress here matters beyond just you, it's how we keep the whole GTM engine strong. The path to AE is real, and for those who put in the work, that next step can come faster than you'd expect elsewhere - with the strength of the peer group you're learning from making all the difference.</p><h2>Who you are</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've got a strong why. Whatever got you here - sport, a career switch, a BDR track record that deserved the promotion you didn't get last time, you know exactly what you're chasing, and that's what gets you through the hard days.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cold calling doesn't scare you. A "no" doesn't ruin your afternoon, it's just the next dial.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're genuinely curious about people. You want to know what's keeping a VP of Engineering up at night, not just whether they'll take a meeting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can write. Not novels, just outreach someone actually wants to open and reply to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You run toward the hard thing. Given the choice between the easy route and the challenging one, you take the challenging one, because you know that's where the bigger payoff is.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're always looking for a better way to work, and that includes using AI properly, testing new tools and workflows, not just running the same playbook because it's familiar.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Startup life suits you. Things change, the odd thing is on fire, and you're fine figuring it out as you go with people around to help.</p></li></ul><h2>Supporting you</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work hard and we think life outside work matters just as much. Our benefits pack is built to support both.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Private medical insurance.</strong> Seriously good cover — we want you and the people you love to be looked after.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive annual leave.</strong> Showing up at your best requires switching off, and we make sure you have time to do that.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First Friday of every month off.</strong> Yes, seriously.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enhanced pension.</strong> We put real money in, because future-you deserves better than an afterthought.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meaningful equity.</strong> We're rapidly scaling, and everyone who helps shape the outcome should share in it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unlimited AI spend.</strong> For everyone, not just engineers. We're all-in on AI across the company, and we expect you to be too.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Generous parental leave.</strong> The early days with a new baby matter more than anything we're doing here, and we want you to be present for them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Two budgets that have your back.</strong> £1000 to invest in your setup, £500 a year to invest in yourself.</p></li></ul><hr><p>Compensation: £65K – £70K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • £65K – £70K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/incidentio/business-development-representative-london-470568","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793958015},{"slug":"account-executive-london-493820","company_name":"incident.io","title":"Account Executive","description":"<h1>A little about us</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://incident.io">incident.io</a> is the AI software reliability platform trusted by engineering teams at Notion, Linear, Ramp and 2,000+ companies who can't afford downtime.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The stakes are real, the talent is insane, and somehow it's a genuinely lovely place to work. We all pull our weight, go the extra mile, and put in the bit of magic most companies don't have time for, all while having fun and never taking ourselves too seriously.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've raised $100+ million from Index Ventures, Insight Partners, and Point Nine, and we're growing fast. There's never been a better time to join.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1>The role in one line</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial AE is where <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://incident.io">incident.io</a>'s growth gets made real - you're in front of the most ambitious digital-native companies out there, and the deals you close show up in the trajectory of the whole business.</p><h2>What that looks like day to day</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a full-cycle AE role with a strong outbound bias. Yes, inbound comes in - but the AEs who thrive here are the ones who don't wait for it. You'll own your own pipeline from the ground up, building target lists, running creative outreach campaigns, and picking up the phone without being asked twice. Outbound here is a craft, not a numbers game.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be selling into VP Engineering, CTO, and SRE leaders at some of the most forward-thinking digital-native companies in the world. Deals typically land in the $40k–$50k range with a clear path into six figures, and a sales cycle of around 45 days means you're moving fast and closing regularly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We run a pod model - you'll work closely with a BDR and Solutions Engineer rather than whoever happens to be free. That means real partnerships, shared context, and accountability that goes both ways. You'll also work alongside CS from early in the deal, which means handoffs that don't lose the thread.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What makes the selling here different is the product and the story behind it. <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://incident.io">incident.io</a> is an AI-native platform built by engineers, for engineers - our founders have been on-call, they've felt the 2am page, and they built something to fix it. When you're in a room with a CTO or an SRE lead, you're not pitching software - you're talking to someone about a problem they've lived, and you understand it. That's the edge.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AEs here are AI-forward in how they operate - whether that's building business cases, running research, or finding smarter ways to work a territory. We expect you to bring ideas, not just execute a playbook.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The progression is real. Commercial AEs have moved into Enterprise and into management - and we'll be straight with you about what the path looks like and what it takes to get there.</p><h2>Who you are</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've closed deals at a similar size and pace before - $40k–$50k ACV, sub-60-day cycles - and you've got the numbers to back it up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Outbound doesn't feel like a chore to you. You see it as a craft - you build your own lists, think creatively about how to get in front of the right people, and don't rely on a sequence template to do the work for you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're genuinely curious about what it's like to be an on-call engineer. Not just the technical side - the stress, the 2am pages, the pressure of being the person whose job it is to fix things fast. That empathy shows up in how you sell.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can hold a technical conversation without leaning on your SE every time. You'll have support when you need it, but you're comfortable going deep on your own.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're scrappy in the best sense - you don't wait for resources, you figure it out. A bigger company with more tools, more inbound, and more hand-holding would actually frustrate you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You pick up the phone. Cold calling doesn't make you wince, and a voicemail doesn't derail your afternoon.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Startup life genuinely appeals to you - not as a stepping stone, but because you want to be somewhere your work is visible and your impact is real.</p></li></ul><h2>Supporting you</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work hard and we think life outside work matters just as much. Our benefits pack is built to support both.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Private medical insurance.</strong> Seriously good cover, we want you and the people you love to be looked after.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive annual leave.</strong> Showing up at your best requires switching off, and we make sure you have time to do that.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First Friday of every month off.</strong> Yes, seriously.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enhanced pension.</strong> We put real money in, because future-you deserves better than an afterthought.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Meaningful equity.</strong> We're rapidly scaling, and everyone who helps shape the outcome should share in it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unlimited AI spend.</strong> For everyone, not just engineers. We're all-in on AI across the company, and we expect you to be too.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Generous parental leave.</strong> The early days with a new baby matter more than anything we're doing here, and we want you to be present for them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Two budgets that have your back.</strong> £1000 to invest in your setup, £500 a year to invest in yourself.</p></li></ul><hr><p>Compensation: £155K – £170K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • £155K – £170K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/incidentio/account-executive-london-493820","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793958015},{"slug":"global-pr-operations-lead-12-month-ftc-london-80788","company_name":"Eb485598 6Bf3 40A5 8560 D70150131305","title":"Global PR Operations Lead - 12 month FTC","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Skyscanner</strong><br /><br />Everyone loves travelling, but planning is not without its challenges ✈️. That's why we've spent 20 years building tools that turn travel-planning chaos into a breeze. Today, around 160 million travellers count on us every month to skip the whole “47 browser tabs open” phase and find flights, cars, and hotels quickly and easily 💻.<br /><br />Joining Skyscanner means becoming part of a global brand that's striving to become the planet's go-to travel hack accessible for all 🌍.<br /><br />Our vision? To be the world's number one travel ally. (Ambitious? 💪Yes, but, hey, that's what got us here).<br /><br />Now, we’re on the lookout for a <strong>Global PR Lead </strong>to help us bring that vision to even more travellers.<br /><br /><strong>About the role</strong><br /><strong>(Hybrid)</strong><br /><br />This is a role at the heart of our fast-paced, high-volume PR team, helping keep our communications flying in formation across 23 markets worldwide. You’ll be the central point connecting plans, people, budgets, agencies and operations — making sure our global PR machine runs smoothly, efficiently and at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working closely with our Senior Director of Communications, regional PR leads, internal teams and global agency partners, you’ll help turn our international PR strategy into coordinated action. From shaping global initiatives to sharpening the way we plan, measure and operate, you’ll bring the structure that helps brilliant PR ideas travel further.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll be doing</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Driving global PR planning:</strong> You’ll lead the planning process with our global PR agency hub, partnering with the Senior Director of Communications to keep forecasting, budgets, resources and priorities aligned.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turning measurement into momentum:</strong> You’ll work closely with our measurement lead to make sure reporting is accurate, useful and connected to the strategies and decisions that matter.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Optimising our PR ecosystem:</strong> You’ll partner with Procurement and Finance to make sure we have the right suppliers, commercial setup and financial tracking in place to support growth — without the spreadsheet drama.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Keeping priorities moving:</strong> You’ll traffic-manage inbound requests, help the team navigate competing priorities and make sure resources are focused where they can have the greatest impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leading global PR initiatives:</strong> You’ll spearhead strategic PR initiatives and special projects beyond our core campaigns, while supporting the delivery of our Awareness strategy and Big Bet activity through PR.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Making operations smarter:</strong> You’ll lead and collaborate on cross-functional improvements spanning tools and technology, including Tableau, ThoughtSpot, AI and our Product Ops model — finding smarter ways for a global team to work at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Creating consistency across markets:</strong> You’ll partner with market leads, our global agency hub and Corporate and B2B PR teams to develop playbooks, strengthen processes and drive consistent adoption and delivery across 23 markets. You’ll also manage and develop our PR Coordinator, keeping calendars, finance trackers and reporting firmly on course.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Global PR operator:</strong> You’ve worked in complex, international communications environments and know how to turn lots of moving parts into one joined-up plan.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategic and operational:</strong> You’re equally comfortable shaping a global PR initiative and getting into the detail needed to make it happen. Big picture, meet beautifully organised spreadsheet.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stakeholder savvy:</strong> You build trusted relationships across senior leaders, market teams, agencies and cross-functional partners, bringing people together around shared priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Agency confident:</strong> You know how to get the best from global agency relationships, balancing clear direction, strong partnership and accountability for delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commercially switched-on:</strong> You’re comfortable working with budgets, forecasting, suppliers, Procurement and Finance, and you understand how strong operational foundations help teams achieve more.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tech and data curious:</strong> You’re interested in how measurement, dashboards, AI and smarter tools can improve PR operations, reporting and decision-making at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Calm in the whirlwind:</strong> You thrive in fast-paced environments, can prioritise when everything feels important, and enjoy helping teams work more effectively. You’re also comfortable managing and developing others along the way.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>What it's like here</strong><br /><br />We are the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.skyscanner.net/jobs/life">real deal -</a> no corporate gloss, no empty promises. Just a team of genuinely curious, caring humans ❤️, building things that help travellers explore the world a little easier 🧭.<br /><br />Skyscanner is made up of brilliant humans from every corner of the world. We believe travel makes the world better - and that the same is true of our diverse teams. We're proud to be an equal opportunities employer and are committed to building an <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.skyscanner.net/jobs/esg">inclusive workplace where everyone can thrive and products that are accessible to all</a> ✨.<br /><br />Sound like your kind of adventure? 🚀 Apply now and help us shape the future of travel.<br /><br /><em>We're committed to ensuring our application and recruitment processes are inclusive and accessible to everyone. If you require any reasonable adjustments or accommodations for interviews, and/or wish to apply under the </em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.skyscanner.net/news/a-disability-confident-employer"><em>Disability Confident</em></a><em> scheme, please let your recruiter know. If you’d like more information on any of our policies, such as hybrid working or Parental Leave policies (typically we pay a minimum of 24 weeks birth parent/maternity leave globally), our recruitment team can provide more information on these.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/eb485598-6bf3-40a5-8560-d70150131305/global-pr-operations-lead-12-month-ftc-london-80788","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Contract"],"location":"London","created_at":1793958015},{"slug":"product-engineer-london-272010","company_name":"hyperexponential","title":"Product Engineer","description":"<h1><strong>About hyperexponential (hx)</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">At hyperexponential, we're building the AI-powered platform that enables the world's most critical decisions in a $7 trillion industry - which risks to take, and how to price them. These are the decisions that shape real-world outcomes: whether rockets successfully launch into space, autonomous vehicles make it to market, or communities recover after major storms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Until now, insurance has been making billion-dollar decisions using outdated tools. We're changing that. Our platform brings together data, AI, and human expertise to give insurers the fastest path from submission to decision - helping them move faster, act smarter, and take on more risk with confidence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by a16z, Highland Europe, and Battery Ventures, we're scaling globally - already trusted by nearly 50 of the world's largest insurers, with zero churn and billions in premiums flowing through hx.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What began as a single product in one market has rapidly evolved into a multi-product, multi-territory platform powering every stage of pricing and underwriting. AI is at the core of what we do - from building the world's first domain-specific AI peer programmer for insurance (think GitHub Copilot with a PhD in actuarial science) to shaping agentic workflows that reinvent how this industry operates.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What makes hx different is the people who build it. Here, impact isn't tied to title or tenure; it's defined by the challenges you take on and the discipline you bring. Surrounded by peers who stretch you, you'll do the best, hardest work of your life in a company engineered to endure.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If that sounds like you, join us in building what comes next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>How we work</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're in the middle of a deliberate shift in how hx builds. Everyone in product development is a <strong>Builder</strong>, and the Product Engineer is the default unit of how we work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We organise around problems, not permanent teams. Small <strong>pods</strong>, usually of two to four Product Engineers, form around the highest-value problem, own it end-to-end from discovery through to running it in production, and re-form as priorities change. Pods sit inside value streams, each owning a customer outcome and led by a <strong>Stream Lead</strong> who decides which problems the stream takes on and holds the bar for what ships. Your growth sits elsewhere: a <strong>Career Mentor </strong>owns your development and progression, so you can move to where the most important problem is without your career following the org chart.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire Product Engineers into hx, not into a fixed team, domain, or layer of the stack. You'll start in the stream where your strengths and our highest-value problems meet, and move as the problems move.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product Engineers are T-shaped: deep expertise in software engineering, plus enough product and design judgement to make routine calls yourself. An embedded PM or designer raises a pod's ceiling on the hardest problems, but is never a gate between you and the customer. This is also a deliberately <strong>AI-native</strong> role, and one of the areas where we're moving fastest.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">A pod of three owns its problem whole, which means going wherever it leads: front end, back end, data, or infrastructure. You don't need to be full-stack by trade, but you do need to be comfortable working outside your strongest layer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Product Engineer role is the same at every level. What scales is the size of the problem you own, how expensive your decisions are to reverse, and how far your judgement travels beyond your pod. At <strong>Level 2</strong>, that looks like this:</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What you'll be doing</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Taking a customer problem from discovery to production inside a pod, getting close to customers yourself, framing the problem, and shipping in small increments guided by real customer signal rather than internal opinion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Directing AI agents to draft implementation, tests, and migrations, then reviewing, integrating, and hardening that work. You'll write intent precisely enough to brief both a teammate and an agent, and own correctness and maintainability regardless of how the first draft was produced.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Designing and delivering robust production systems where correctness, performance, and resource efficiency matter, with the tests and observability that make complex behaviour safe to evolve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working across the codebase wherever the problem leads, including areas your pod doesn't steward, with stewards looped in proportionate to the risk rather than handing work off and waiting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Moving between pods, problems, and streams as priorities change, ramping fast on unfamiliar domains and leaving what you built running well behind you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Taking full accountability for outcomes rather than just your code changes: raising risks early, and deciding rather than escalating.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll need to have done</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Built and shipped production systems end-to-end, from design through rollout, monitoring, and iteration, in settings where correctness, performance, and resource efficiency mattered.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Designed testing and observability that made complex behaviour understandable, debuggable, and safe to evolve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Worked effectively in a polyglot environment, choosing the right tool for the problem and picking up unfamiliar languages, domains, and codebases fast. Strong systems experience, for example in Rust, C/C++, or Python, is valued, and we'll upskill you where there are gaps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shipped work outside your strongest layer of the stack when the problem needed it, picking up the front end, the data layer, or the infrastructure rather than waiting for someone else to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Used AI tools as a serious part of how you build, with the judgement to direct, review, and stand behind what they produce.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Carried product and design judgement into your engineering work, shaping the solution rather than only implementing a spec and making sensible calls under ambiguity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owned outcomes beyond your immediate task, taking decisions rather than escalating them.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>You’re unlikely to thrive here if</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You prefer following detailed instructions rather than experimenting and finding your own approach.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are uncomfortable working directly with non-technical stakeholders to understand their challenges.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You avoid tackling ambiguous or open-ended problems where the solution isn’t obvious.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">If reading our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://hx.wiki/"><strong><u>Culture Document</u></strong></a> leaves you feeling neutral rather than energised, hx may not be the place where you’ll do your best work. We’re building something that asks for commitment and conviction, and we want you to feel excited by the opportunity to grow with us.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Compensation</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At hx, we’re committed to salary transparency. You’ll always have clarity on pay early in the process - our Talent Partner will share details with you during initial conversations - and we’re working towards publishing salary information for all roles globally.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Because we’re building at the intersection of technology/SaaS and insurance, our roles don’t always map neatly onto traditional benchmarks. Our approach is to design compensation that’s competitive in the market, fair across teams, and aligned with the impact our people make.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Benefits</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">£5,000 training and conference budget for individual and group development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days of holiday plus 8 bank holidays (33 days total).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company pension scheme via Penfold.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mental health support and therapy via <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Spectrum.life">Spectrum.life</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Individual wellbeing allowance via Juno.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private healthcare insurance through AXA.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Income protection and Life Insurance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Interview process</h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Initial chat with our Talent team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead Hirer Interview</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Live AI Skills Assessment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Values Interview with the CPTO</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meet the CEO</p></li></ol><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>Our commitment to Diversity</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">hxers are at the centre of everything we build. We know that progress depends on diverse perspectives, and we are committed to creating an environment where everyone can thrive, grow, and make an impact. We recognise there is always more to do, and we take responsibility for shaping a workplace that is not only diverse but genuinely inclusive.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Diversity is not just the right thing to do, it is key to solving the complex challenges we choose t