uct-engineer-london-174396","company_name":"hyperexponential","title":"Staff Product Engineer","description":"<h1><strong>About hyperexponential (hx)</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">At hyperexponential, we're building the AI-powered platform that enables the world's most critical decisions in a $7 trillion industry - which risks to take, and how to price them. These are the decisions that shape real-world outcomes: whether rockets successfully launch into space, autonomous vehicles make it to market, or communities recover after major storms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Until now, insurance has been making billion-dollar decisions using outdated tools. We're changing that. Our platform brings together data, AI, and human expertise to give insurers the fastest path from submission to decision - helping them move faster, act smarter, and take on more risk with confidence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by a16z, Highland Europe, and Battery Ventures, we're scaling globally - already trusted by nearly 50 of the world's largest insurers, with zero churn and billions in premiums flowing through hx.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What began as a single product in one market has rapidly evolved into a multi-product, multi-territory platform powering every stage of pricing and underwriting. AI is at the core of what we do - from building the world's first domain-specific AI peer programmer for insurance (think GitHub Copilot with a PhD in actuarial science) to shaping agentic workflows that reinvent how this industry operates.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What makes hx different is the people who build it. Here, impact isn't tied to title or tenure; it's defined by the challenges you take on and the discipline you bring. Surrounded by peers who stretch you, you'll do the best, hardest work of your life in a company engineered to endure.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If that sounds like you, join us in building what comes next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>How we work</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're in the middle of a deliberate shift in how hx builds. Everyone in product development is a <strong>Builder</strong>, and the Product Engineer is the default unit of how we work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We organise around problems, not permanent teams. Small <strong>pods</strong>, usually of two to four Product Engineers, form around the highest-value problem, own it end-to-end from discovery through to running it in production, and re-form as priorities change. Pods sit inside value streams, each owning a customer outcome and led by a <strong>Stream Lead</strong> who decides which problems the stream takes on and holds the bar for what ships. Your growth sits elsewhere: a <strong>Career Mentor </strong>owns your development and progression, so you can move to where the most important problem is without your career following the org chart.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We hire Product Engineers into hx, not into a fixed team, domain, or layer of the stack. You'll start in the stream where your strengths and our highest-value problems meet, and move as the problems move.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product Engineers are T-shaped: deep expertise in software engineering, plus enough product and design judgement to make routine calls yourself. An embedded PM or designer raises a pod's ceiling on the hardest problems, but is never a gate between you and the customer. This is also a deliberately <strong>AI-native</strong> role, and one of the areas where we're moving fastest.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">A pod of three owns its problem whole, which means going wherever it leads: front end, back end, data, or infrastructure. You don't need to be full-stack by trade, but you do need to be comfortable working outside your strongest layer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Product Engineer role is the same at every level. What scales is the size of the problem you own, how expensive y