ases, customer feedback and team capacity. Use that information to prioritise improvements and make clear recommendations about investment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing and developing a technical support or support engineering team serving business customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of improving both customer outcomes and how a support function operates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical understanding of APIs, HTTP, authentication, webhooks and integrations, with enough practical depth to guide investigations and earn the trust of engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort working with logs, SQL and scripts to investigate problems or improve support workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience handling consequential customer escalations, including situations where the cause or resolution is initially uncertain.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to explain technical issues to developers, business stakeholders and senior leaders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sound judgement about urgency, customer impact and competing priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evidence of effective hiring, coaching, performance management and delegation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to influence Product, Engineering and commercial teams through clear reasoning and useful evidence.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort building and improving a function in a growing company, while remaining involved in its day-to-day work.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Experience that would be useful</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Supporting an API platform, developer product or infrastructure business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working with enterprise customers running important production integrations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leading support across different time zones.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improving support tooling, knowledge management, self-service or automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in travel technology, payments or another industry with complex external dependencies.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>You don’t need to have worked in travel or held this exact title. We’re interested in the teams you’ve developed, the problems you’ve solved and the judgement you bring.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What success looks like</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">During your first six months:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engineers have clear expectations, regular coaching and practical development plans.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer issues have clear ownership, appropriate prioritisation and dependable communication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have established a trustworthy baseline for support performance and delivered measurable improvements in the most important areas.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Escalations reach the right teams with better evidence and fewer unnecessary handovers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recurring problems are being addressed through product changes, documentation or tooling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Duffel has a clear plan for the support capacity and capabilities needed as the business grows.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why You’ll Love Working at Duffel</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe in true ownership. That’s why every permanent employee gets equity in the business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Perks That Actually Matter:</st