lders</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We'd love to hear from you if you have...🔍</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in a tech and/or consumer-oriented industry, comfortable with a fast-paced business</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of leading projects end to end and getting the right stakeholders involved to keep things moving</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A curious, analytical mindset, with confidence developing hypotheses, briefing research and using data and insight to guide decisions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort managing and communicating with senior stakeholders, including Execs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Naturally organised, with experience managing multiple propositions from development through to delivery</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong familiarity with both brand and business performance KPIs</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working within or alongside product marketing teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">It's helpful if you have exposure to AI tools and/or have experience across international European markets, though none of these are dealbreakers</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>More information:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enjoy fantastic perks like private healthcare &amp; dental insurance, a generous work from abroad policy, 2-for-1 share purchase plans, an EV Scheme to further reduce carbon emissions, extra festive time off, and excellent family-friendly benefits. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We prioritise career growth with clear career paths, transparent pay bands, personal learning budgets, and regular learning days. Jump on board and supercharge your career from day one! </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're operating a hybrid model and ask that Trainliners work from the office a minimum of 60% of their time over a 12-week period. We also have a 28-day Work from Abroad policy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our values represent the things that matter most to us and what we live and breathe everyday, in everything we do: </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">💭 <strong>Think Big</strong> - We're building the future of rail </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">✔️ <strong>Own It </strong>- We focus on every customer, partner and journey </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">🤝 <strong> Travel Together</strong> - We're one team </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">♻️<strong> Do Good</strong> - We make a positive impact </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">We know that having a diverse team makes us better and helps us succeed. And we mean all forms of diversity - gender, ethnicity, sexuality, disability, nationality and diversity of thought. That's why we're committed to creating inclusive places to work, where everyone belongs and differences are valued and celebrated.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interested in finding out more about what it's like to work at Trainline? Why not check us out on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/trainline/">LinkedIn</a>, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.instagram.com/lifeattrainline/">Instagram</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.glassdoor.co.uk/Overview/Working-at-Trainline-EI_IE249203.11,20.htm">Glassdoor</a>! </p><hr><p>Compensation: £65K – £72K • Offers Bonus</p><ul><li> • £65K – £72K • Offers Bonus</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/trainline/brand-proposition-lead-london-302698","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793958014},{"slug":"product-analyst-london-38571","company_name":"Accurx","title":"Product Analyst","description":"<h2><strong><u>London/Hybrid</u></strong></h2><h2><strong><u>£40,000 - £60,000 + share options up to £14,500 +</u></strong><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.notion.so/accurx/Perks-Benefits-f1e9148b71be486791aa2c503e5d775a?source=copy_link"><strong><u> Benefits</u></strong></a></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>💬 Accurx is where conversations happen with and about patients.</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">For decades, the NHS has struggled with fragmented systems that make simple tasks feel impossible. We’re changing that by building a single, system-wide platform that connects everyone through communication.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What started as a way for GPs to text a patient has now evolved into an all-in-one digital toolkit used by 98% of GP practices.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our platform now powers <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.accurx.com/primary-care">Total Triage</a> to manage patient demand, and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.accurx.com/booking">Self-Book,</a><strong> </strong>which lets patients schedule their own appointments in seconds. We’ve automated routine care with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.accurx.com/questionnaires">Patient Questionnaires</a> for long-term conditions, while <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.accurx.com/accumail">Accumail</a> finally allows staff-to-staff communication to happen instantly across different care settings. We’re now pushing the boundaries of the consultation itself with <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.accurx.com/scribe">Accurx Scribe</a>, our AI-powered note-taker that drafts medical notes in real-time.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>The team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We have a massive vision and even more ideas, but right now, our ambitions are outstripping our capacity. That’s where you come in. We aren't looking for someone to just "run the reports" we’re looking for a foundational member of a growing function who is excited to help us redefine how data influences product.<br /><br />At Accurx, we don't just wait for a roadmap to be handed down; we expect everyone to help shape it. While you'll be part of a team of expert data and product leaders, you'll be the one in the driver's seat for your domain. You won't be watching from the sidelines - you'll be proactively hunting for insights, challenging our current assumptions, and taking ownership of how data can save clinician time from day one. This is a role for a critical thinker who is energised by the "blank canvas" of a growing function and has the drive to turn raw data into a better reality for millions of patients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Challenges you’ll solve...</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will steer product strategy by partnering with Product Managers to define what success looks like and by monitoring the KPIs that prove our impact on the frontline of healthcare.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will interrogate user behaviour by performing deep-dive analyses that look past the surface to find the "why," ensuring we’re solving the right problems for the right people.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will lead rigorous experiments by helping design and run A/B tests, owning the process from the initial hypothesis through to the final, data-backed recommendation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will build the engine for self-service insights by creating the dashboards and visualisations that ensure your pod has high-quality data at their fingertips to move fast.</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>You should apply if...</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You've worked within a product team environment</strong> (not just as a standalone data or BI function), partnering directly with Product Managers, Engineers, and Designers on live product decisions, not just reporting on outcomes after the fact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a proactive investigator who doesn't need a ticket to start digging; when things are quiet, you’re already looking for the next trend or bottleneck that we’ve missed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a "get stuck in" mindset - you’re excited by a lean environment where you can build your own processes and take on challenges that push you outside your comfort zone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring strong Product Thinking with an understanding of user funnels and a hunger to master metrics like activation, retention, and cohort behaviour.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are sharpening a strong technical toolkit, with a solid command of SQL and the ambition to use Python.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are a delivery-focused collaborator who thrives in agile environments and knows how to communicate technical findings clearly to engineers and designers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve used tools like Mixpanel or Amplitude and are ready to become a power user who empowers the whole team through effective data storytelling.</p></li></ul><h3></h3><h2><strong>What’s in it for you?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll join a high-performing team on a mission to solve healthcare productivity, building a platform used by around 300k NHS staff every week, supporting the care of over 50 million NHS patients every year. We set a high bar, move fast, and give people the ownership and support to do the best work of their careers</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>£40,000 - £60,000 salary,</strong> plus a discretionary recognition bonus for exceptional performance and impact, nominated by managers and awarded by our leadership team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equity:</strong> £14,500 in equal share options, so you share in the value you help create</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits to suit you:</strong> adjust your healthcare cover, your pension or life insurance, whatever stage you’re at in life</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Built for collaboration: </strong>We are an office-first culture and ask that you’re in our (dog-friendly) Shoreditch office for a minimum of 3 days a week</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Close to our users:</strong> Regular hackathons, plus dedicated time to visit GP practices and other healthcare settings to see first-hand how our products are used</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time off: </strong>You’ll get 28 days of holiday (plus bank holidays) and up to 4 weeks to work from anywhere per year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Support at home: </strong>We offer enhanced parental leave, fertility support and parental loss support</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We have our very own chefs:</strong> Free healthy breakfasts, snacks and lunches, plus a weekly sweet treat</p></li></ul><hr><p>Compensation: £40K – £60K • Offers Equity</p><ul><li> • £40K – £60K • Offers Equity</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/accurx/product-analyst-london-38571","tags":["Product & Technology"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London (Shoreditch)","created_at":1793958013},{"slug":"data-engineering-manager-data-platform-london-477264","company_name":"Fundingcircle","title":"Data Engineering Manager (Data Platform)","description":"<h2><strong>We’re on a mission to back the UK’s small businesses like no one else</strong> 🚀</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Small businesses are the backbone of the economy, and we’re here to help them win. We’ve built a platform that uses clever data to get them the funding they need in minutes, not weeks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Funding Circle, we have the restless energy of a fintech start-up with the stability of a public company. It’s a unique mix that gives Circlers the autonomy to take ownership and the scale to make an impact that truly counts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re a high-performing team that chooses to lift each other up. We challenge, we champion, and we have each other’s backs -  because we know that when we stand together, we move faster and build better.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The impact is real:</strong> Last year alone, the businesses on our platform generated £7.2bn for the UK economy 📈 <strong>Come and join a mission that matters!</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">[<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.fundingcircle.com/uk/impact"><u>Read our Impact Report</u></a>] | [<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://uk.trustpilot.com/review/fundingcircle.com"><u>See our Trustpilot</u></a>]</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The role ⚡</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">📍 London (Hybrid) | 🤝 2 days in the office | 💰 Competitive Salary + Benefits<br /><br />You’ll make a real difference for our customers and your team from day one. We believe the fastest way to grow is by doing, so we give you the ownership to run with things and see real-time results.<br /><br />We are looking for a Data Platform Engineering Manager to join our Data Platform Engineering team which sits under Tech and Data. We’re partway through a migration to a modern Snowflake-based platform, so you’ll join at a pivotal point where your decisions will shape how we work for years to come<br /><br />Reporting directly to the Head of Data Engineering, You’ll partner closely with our Technical Lead and Principal Engineer: while they drive architecture and technical patterns, you will own the delivery engine, team health, career progression, and stakeholder alignment that turns strategy into reality.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead, manage, and mentor a team of data platform engineers, fostering a collaborative, innovative, and inclusive team culture.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Champion a product mindset for internal tooling, ensuring our platform empowers domain teams to build quickly and safely without bottlenecks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee the recruitment, onboarding, and performance management processes for the team. Set clear goals and expectations, providing regular feedback and guidance to team members.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Oversee the planning, execution, and delivery of projects within the data platform roadmap, ensuring timely and high-quality outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the team's backlog, prioritise tasks effectively. Define and track key performance indicators (KPIs) for platform health and team delivery.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build strong relationships and collaborate effectively with key stakeholders, including technical and business leaders. Understand stakeholder needs and translate them into actionable requirements for the data platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicate the team's roadmap, progress, challenges, and successes clearly and proactively to technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Actively invest in the career development of your team members through coaching, mentoring, and identifying growth opportunities. Create personalised development plans and support engineers in acquiring new skills and expertise. Foster a culture of continuous learning, knowledge sharing, and technical curiosity within the team.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2>What we’re looking for 🌱</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We value deep expertise, but a growth mindset and good energy are what really make our team click. We’re a group that chooses to lift each other up and think smart every day.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solid understanding of modern data platform architectures (,e.g. Snowflake, data mesh/lakehouse, dbt, Airflow, streaming vs. batch pipelines, data contracts)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience managing and leading high-performing data engineering teams in a product-driven environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of mentoring and developing engineers, fostering a culture of technical excellence, innovation, and professional growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrable experience in managing project delivery, including planning, prioritisation, and execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with Agile/Scrum methodologies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent stakeholder management and communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with both technical and non-technical audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Able to architect custom AI solutions and smart automated systems that are safe, maintainable, and aligned with our long-term mission</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a technical bridge and mentor, training  “builders" across the company to move from basic AI usage to sophisticated system creation</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Skills we’d love to see:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience shaping data platform strategy and vision, aligning technical capabilities with evolving business needs and helping drive technical innovation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A proactive approach to identifying and implementing improvements related to platform reliability, scalability, performance, and cost.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience running a platform team that serves internal customers, with a focus on self-service and developer experience.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We’re building a place where everyone truly feels they belong. Even if your past experience doesn't align perfectly with every requirement, we'd still love to hear from you.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why join us? 💜</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We back you to build an incredible career and by joining us, you'll be part of one of <strong>The Sunday Times Best Companies to Work For 2026</strong>! As a flexible-first employer, we use a "best of both" approach. We’ll see you in our London office to collaborate – with barista coffee and subsidised Just Eat lunches on us!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Circler Proposition focuses on five areas:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Flexibility:</strong> We provide a benefit allowance you can tailor to your own life and family.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Health:</strong> This includes private medical and dental, health assessments, and access to a digital GP.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Wealth:</strong> We offer life assurance, share schemes, and financial coaching.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Development:</strong> You get a dedicated annual learning allowance to help you level up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lifestyle:</strong> We have electric car and cycle-to-work schemes, plus season ticket loans.</p>