ng manufacturing systems across our sites, a significant focus will be on digital transformation projects, data analytics, machine optimisation and emerging technologies, including AI and machine learning. You'll also play an important role in supporting major business initiatives and helping shape the future of manufacturing technology across KP Snacks.</p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>What’s in it for you?</strong><br>We believe in rewarding our colleagues and helping them thrive. Here’s a flavour of what we offer:</p><ul><li><p>Competitive annual salary, annual salary review and annual bonus opportunity (target 5%)</p></li><li><p>Business needs car allowance </p></li><li><p>KP Pension Plan with up to 7% matched contributions</p></li><li><p>25 days holiday, with the option to buy up to five additional days, plus additional holiday after five years’ service</p></li><li><p>Comprehensive healthcare including Single Cover Private Healthcare, Health Cash Plan, Digital GP and Employee Assistance Programme</p></li><li><p>Electric Vehicle Car Scheme, supporting more sustainable and cost-effective travel</p></li><li><p>KP4ME benefits platform with discounts, cashback and wellbeing support</p></li><li><p>Enhanced family-friendly policies to support colleagues at every stage of life</p></li></ul><p style="text-align:start;min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p style="text-align:start;"><strong>What will you be doing?</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Leading manufacturing systems support and governance</strong><br>Providing technical ownership of key manufacturing systems, ensuring they remain reliable, secure, standardised and aligned to business needs</p></li><li><p><strong>Driving data-led performance improvement</strong><br>Developing dashboards, reporting solutions and performance metrics that improve operational visibility, support decision making and unlock opportunities for continuous improvement</p></li><li><p><strong>Supporting digital transformation projects</strong><br>Leading and supporting projects focused on manufacturing systems, digitisation, machine optimisation and emerging technologies, helping KP Snacks maximise the value of its technology investments</p></li><li><p><strong>Building strong partnerships across the business</strong><br>Working closely with Engineering, Operations, OT, IT and external partners to deliver improvements, resolve complex issues and ensure manufacturing requirements are represented in key projects</p></li><li><p><strong>Developing capability and future ways of working</strong><br>Coaching site-based systems contacts, driving standardisation across sites and supporting the adoption of AI, machine learning and advanced analytics solutions</p></li></ul> <br> <p style="text-align:start;"><strong>We’d love to hear from you if you can bring:</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Manufacturing systems experience</strong><br>Experience supporting Manufacturing Execution Systems (MES) or similar manufacturing technologies within an FMCG, manufacturing or industrial environment</p></li><li><p><strong>Strong data and analytics capability</strong><br>The ability to analyse operational data, create meaningful insights and use reporting tools such as Power BI to support business performance</p></li><li><p><strong>Experience delivering technology improvements</strong><br>A track record of identifying and implementing system enhancements, automation solutions or digital initiatives that deliver measurable business value</p></li><li><p><strong>Excellent stakeholder management skills</strong><br>The ability to build relationships and influence colleagues across Engineering, Operations, OT, IT and external suppliers</p></li><li><p><strong>A passion for innovation and continuous improvement</strong><br>An interest in emerging technologies including AI, machine learning and Industry 4.0, combined with a desire to improve the way manufacturing systems support business performance</p></li><li>