rs, client-facing teams; combining their input with market insight, data and your own judgment to set a clear product direction.</p><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>What you will do</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Strategy and roadmap</strong></p><ul><li><p>Own the product vision and roadmap, aligned with TechOps and company goals.</p></li><li><p>Track the VDR market, competitors and emerging technology (especially AI), and turn insight into prioritized bets.</p></li><li><p>Build business cases with cost, revenue and timeline impact, make clear trade-offs, and explain prioritization and scope changes to stakeholders before they ask.<br></p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Discovery and requirements</strong></p><ul><li><p>Run discovery with clients, deal teams, sales and support to understand real workflows and pain points.</p></li><li><p>Write features and PBIs in Azure DevOps with clear business rules, scope and testable acceptance criteria.</p></li><li><p>Partner with UX design on user-centered solutions for admins, deal managers and external bidders.</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal">&nbsp;</p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Delivery and release</strong></p><ul><li><p>Work with product, engineering and QA to plan sprints, unblock work and keep releases moving.</p></li><li><p>Be the first point of contact for product questions from engineering, QA and UX.</p></li><li><p>Own release readiness, UAT and release notes for every release, including hotfixes.</p></li><li><p>Triage escalations and client-reported issues, and agree priorities with Support.</p></li></ul><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p class="MsoNormal"><strong>Measurement and clients</strong></p><ul><li><p>Define and track product metrics (adoption, time to set up a room, retention, NPS, incident and defect trends), and use product analytics to judge feature performance and guide prioritization.</p></li><li><p>Present to key clients and partners, and