gnificant autonomy and reporting to Gizem Altay, Principal Scientist, you will own the establishment of patient-derived organoids from fresh surgical specimens — starting with NSCLC and extending to additional tumour types — from tissue receipt and dissociation through to stable, well-characterised lines ready for downstream applications. You will develop and optimise robust culture protocols, ensure reproducibility across donors, and generate the high-quality biological models that power our AI predictive engine and our partnerships with hospitals and pharma.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Preferred experience</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Must have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">PhD in cancer biology, molecular biology, cell biology, biotechnology, or a related field, as well as 5+ years of hands-on experience, including industry or translational settings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven, hands-on experience establishing NSCLC patient-derived organoids from fresh surgical specimens — including tissue handling, dissociation, embedding, and long-term expansion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong track record in primary tumour culture, including troubleshooting low take-rates, and donor-to-donor variability and other optimization including: media formulation, matrix selection, passaging strategies, cryopreservation etc.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional wet-lab fundamentals: sterile technique, routine culture, assay development, and QC.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prior experience in building scientific direction, ownership of QC/characterisation strategy, and decision-making</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated ability to independently plan, prioritise, and execute complex experimental pipelines with high quality and reproducibility.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical and quantitative data-interpretation skills, with clear documentation and reporting.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct experience collaborating with hospitals, pathology departments, or surgical teams on biospecimen workflows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with drug-response profiling in organoids (dose–response, time-course, combination assays).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Knowledge of molecular biology techniques and NGS workflows (WES, RNA-seq) for organoid characterisation and tumour-organoid concordance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Previous responsibility for managing CROs or academic collaborations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience mentoring junior scientists or lab technicians, and establishing lab standards.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What will you find at Orakl</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mission: Work in a cutting-edge environment, on the bleeding edge of cancer research.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth opportunities: we’re rapidly expanding the scope of our work and you will be offered multiple opportunities to grow with it!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Impact: you’re going to be participating in a fast-growing, multi-faceted project with multiple opportunities to shape it according to your interests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">More about Orakl <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.welcometothejungle.com/fr/companies/orakl-oncology">on our Welcome to the Jungle page</a> and <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.orakl-oncology.com">on our website</a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Recruitment steps</strong></p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li