d on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE: NU), we combine proprietary technology, data intelligence, and an efficient operating model to deliver financial products that are simple, accessible, and human.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our impact has been recognized by global rankings such as Time 100 Companies, Fast Company’s Most Innovative Companies, and Forbes World’s Best Bank. Visit our institutional page <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://international.nubank.com.br/careers/"><u>https://international.nubank.com.br/careers/</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>About the role</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nu Global AG is Nu's Swiss entity, based in Zug. It went live in October 2026 with its AML/CFT and sanctions framework already in place: entity risk analysis, internal directives, customer risk classification, monitoring and screening standards, and MROS reporting. The same team also drives the next steps of Nu's expansion in Europe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are looking for a senior AML professional to act as deputy to the Head of AML/CFTP &amp; Sanctions. In 2027 you will take over the day to day MLRO duties of the Swiss entity, so the Head of AML can focus on strategy, and you will help take the framework built in Switzerland to new markets in Europe, adapting it to the new EU AML package (AMLR and AMLD6).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will join a small, senior team where everyone owns their decisions and does the work themselves. You will work directly with senior management, the first line, our auditors and our regulators.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>You'll be responsible for</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as deputy to the AML Compliance Officer (MLRO) and stand in whenever needed</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the day to day MLRO activities: escalated cases, decisions on reports to MROS under Art. 9 AMLA through goAML, and sanctions duties towards SECO, including asset freezes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review and challenge the first line: sample based quality assurance of alert handling and case files, and sign off on changes to transaction monitoring rules and screening thresholds</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the framework current: entity risk analysis, internal directives and procedures, and the annual AML/CFT report to the Board</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Issue the financial crime opinion on new products, features and material changes at the Product Risk Committee</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the point of contact for our SRO, MROS, SECO and the external AML auditor, and for due diligence requests from partner and correspondent institutions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the AML/CFT training plan and the training duty under Art. 8 AMLA</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Nu expands in Europe, adapt the Swiss framework to the new EU AML package (AMLR and AMLD6) and turn it into binding control requirements for product, engineering and operations</p></li></ul><h3><strong>We are looking for someone who has</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Served as MLRO, AML Compliance Officer or formal deputy at a regulated financial intermediary in Switzerland, supervised by FINMA or an SRO, or in the EU (mandatory)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lives in Switzerland today (mandatory)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meets the fit and proper requirements that regulators apply to AML officers (mandatory)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Holds the CAMS certification (mandatory)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Speaks fluent English, our working language, and fluent German (mandatory)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Has practical experience with the Swiss AML framework (AMLA, AMLO, FINMA AMLO and SRO rules, MROS and SECO reporting), the EU AML framework, or both, and a working knowledge of the new EU AML package (AMLR and AMLD6)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Has built or set up an AML function or framework</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Has taken and defended reporting and freezing decisions, and has dealt directly with FINMA, SROs, other regulators and external auditors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Has reviewed and challenged first line controls at a senior level: transaction monitoring, sanctions screening, KYC and customer risk classification</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Writes clearly and precisely in policies, opinions and regulatory correspondence</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sanctions expertise: screening, list management, asset freezes and reporting under Swiss and EU sanctions regimes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with international remittances and cross border payments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Travel Rule compliance, including for digital assets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a fintech or in a newly authorised financial institution</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort using data and AI tools to review alerts, test controls and draft documentation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Other certifications such as CGSS, CCAS, Chainalysis Reactor or Chainalysis KYT (recommended)</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Location for this opportunity</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Zug, Switzerland (you must live in Switzerland today)</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Our Benefits</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Chance of earning equity at Nubank</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health Insurance Allowance for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension Plan</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Accident Insurance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Daily Sickness Benefits</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Life Insurance &amp; Death Benefits</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">NuCare – Employee Assistance Programme, available 24/7 for you and your dependents</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">NuLanguage – Language Course Program</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Extended Parental Leave</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">International Travel Insurance for business trips</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work-from-home Allowance and office equipment for working from home</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Parking space at the Zug office</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Work Model for this Role</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hybrid 2-3 times/week</strong>: Our hybrid work model brings us to the office at least twice a week, on strategic days designed to maximize team connection and collaboration. For more details, visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://building.nubank.com/nu-hybrid-work-model/"><u>https://building.nubank.com/nu-hybrid-work-model/</u></a></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our recruitment process may involve the use of artificial intelligence–enabled tools, such as automated interview transcription and analysis, to support the evaluation process. Artificial intelligence is not used to make final hiring decisions; all decisions are made by human reviewers.<br /><br />To maintain a consistent and fair process for every candidate, Nu does not provide individualized technical feedback. See how our policy works <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://script.google.com/a/macros/nubank.com.br/s/AKfycbwvrewE58oGSbRWIVv8CyCWN68GLxpPVsfYYXv-ZHg94QFsTJmi82rF1x0yt-OTs2W0DQ/exec">here</a></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/nubank/deputy-mlro-aml-compliance-zurich-335583","tags":["Enterprise Functions"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1793720434},{"slug":"homologation-certification-engineer-energy-systems-nyon-202443","company_name":"Eh Energy","title":"Homologation & Certification Engineer, Energy Systems","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About EH Energy Engineering</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">EH Energy is developing cutting-edge fuel cell technology for heavy-duty mobility and large-scale stationary power applications. Our uniquely redesigned product delivers a significantly more compact fuel cell system with high power density and lower production costs. In response to the challenges of climate change and the global shift toward decentralized energy, EH Energy provides high-performance, cost-effective fuel cell solutions to our clients and partners.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To support our rapid growth and bring our systems to global markets, we are seeking a Certification Engineer. In this critical role, you will take full ownership of our product compliance roadmap, bridging the gap between innovative engineering and strict global regulations. You will lead hazard and risk assessments, define certification strategies across international markets (EU, North America, marine), and interface directly with notified bodies and classification societies to ensure our fuel cell systems are safe, fully compliant, and market-ready.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role <strong>requires a full-time, on-site presence at our office in Nyon, Switzerland</strong>. We are <strong>unable to offer remote or hybrid arrangements</strong>, so candidates should be based locally or <strong>prepared to relocate</strong>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Key responsibilities</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Certification strategy and project management</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify applicable directives, regulations, harmonised standards and class rules early in the development cycle and translate them into design requirements (EU, North America, marine)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Select and manage notified bodies, NRTLs, classification societies and test laboratories, own budgets, schedules and contracts for certification work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Plan and witness type tests, factory acceptance tests (FAT) and site acceptance tests (SAT)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Safety engineering and risk analysis</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead risk assessments to ISO 12100 and hazard studies (HAZID, HAZOP to IEC 61882)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead design and process FMEA (IEC 60812) for stacks, balance of plant, containers and fuel processing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run explosion-protection assessments: hazardous area classification (IEC 60079-10-1), ventilation and gas detection concepts, and equipment selection</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Specify and verify safety functions to ISO 13849 (PL) and IEC 61508, including safety requirement specifications and validation reports</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compliance and technical documentation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Compile and maintain technical construction files, CE Declarations of Conformity, type-approval dossiers and certification reports</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and review user, installation, operation and maintenance manuals, safety instructions and labelling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain the standards register and assess the impact of new or revised standards</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage certif