li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je stuurt een team van werkstudenten en stagiaires aan en zorgt er samen met hen voor dat alle facturen tijdig en correct worden verwerkt.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je ondersteunt bij de maandafsluiting, controleert grootboekrekeningen en helpt mee met ad-hoc analyses en periodieke rapportages.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je denkt actief mee over het slim inrichten van financiële workflows. Je verkent en implementeert mogelijkheden voor procesautomatisering, slimme datakoppelingen en AI-oplossingen (zoals OCR-herkenning en geautomatiseerde factuurverwerking).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je rapporteert aan de Lead Financial Controller, die je ondersteunt in je dagelijkse werkzaamheden en je helpt om door te groeien in je rol.</p></li></ul><h1>Dit ben jij</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Als ideale kandidaat heb je al een basis aan kennis en ervaring en wil je blijven leren in een vakgebied dat continu verandert en digitaliseert. Je herkent jezelf in het volgende profiel:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je beschikt over een afgeronde hbo- of universitaire opleiding (bijvoorbeeld Finance, Bedrijfseconomie of Accountancy).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je hebt 0-3 jaar relevante werkervaring in een financiële of control-functie.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je hebt ervaring met de crediteurenadministratie en het verwerken en controleren van facturen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kennis van accountingsoftware (zoals Exact) is een pré.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je bent handig met data en hebt een sterke affiniteit met automatisering en nieuwe technologieën (zoals AI-tools, data-integraties en procesoptimalisatie).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je schrijft en spreekt vloeiend Nederlands en Engels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je bent integer, nauwkeurig en risicobewust. Je begrijpt dat een strakke administratie de basis vormt voor goede besluitvorming.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Je denkt in kansen en mogelijkheden: je ziet direct waar processen sneller, slimmer of foutlozer kunnen en schroomt niet om dit op te pakken.</p></li></ul><h1>Wat wij bieden</h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Werken bij een B Corp gecertificeerd bedrijf, waarbij je de kans krijgt om je stempel te drukken op het Europese voedselsysteem.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">27 vakantiedagen om bij te komen en op te laden.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Een extra vrije dag per jaar om je in te zetten voor vrijwilligerswerk en iets goeds te doen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aandacht voor je mentale gezondheid met online begeleiding van erkende psychologen via OpenUp.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Voor straks een perfect pensioen via BPFL.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Elke maand food for thought, met workshops en talks via de Crisp University.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regelmatig tastings of workshops op kantoor of bij een van onze leveranciers, om te zien hoe onze lekkerste producten worden gemaakt – en natuurlijk ook te proeven.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dagelijks een uitgebreide, georganiseerde lunch op kantoor.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enthousiaste, slimme collega’s en tijd om elkaar te leren kennen tijdens sport, events en proeverijen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">En... fikse korting op je Crisp boodschappen, omdat je thuis natuurlijk ook goed wilt eten.</p></li></ul><h1>Onze selectieprocedure</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solliciteer via onderstaande button. Hoe meer je kunt delen over jezelf en de reden dat je solliciteert, hoe beter.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bij Crisp streven we naar een inclusieve en diverse werkomgeving waarin iedereen welkom is, ongeacht hun achtergrond, geslacht, leeftijd, etniciteit, seksuele geaardheid, religie of beperking. Wij moedigen sollicitanten met diverse perspectieven en achtergronden aan om te solliciteren en geloven in gelijke kansen voor iedereen. We waarderen de unieke bijdragen die elke medewerker kan leveren en zijn vastbesloten om een inclusieve werkplek te creëren waarin iedereen wordt gerespecteerd en gewaardeerd.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/crisp/accounts-payable-financial-controller-amsterdam-141044","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1793731236},{"slug":"audit-methodology-lead-amsterdam-344115","company_name":"Datasnipper","title":"Audit Methodology Lead","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">We build AI agents that perform audit procedures for audit firms. We need an experienced auditor to decide what correct output from those agents looks like, and whether our agents meet that bar.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll join one of our product groups as its audit expert. You'll write the criteria and reference cases our agents are tested against, review agent output the way you'd review a file, and tell the team plainly when something isn't ready for a live engagement. You'll use AI to create realistic test material, and you'll review all of it yourself.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About DataSnipper</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>The hardest AI problems aren't about getting an answer fast. They're about getting one people can trust.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe trust is essential to how society works. Every day, we rely on information that's been independently verified, from financial statements to the products we buy, to the sustainability claims companies make. Behind that trust are audit and finance professionals who examine evidence, verify information and hold organizations accountable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At DataSnipper, we build AI solutions that empower those professionals. By making evidence easier to trace and verify, we help them focus on the judgment and expertise that make their work so important.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>For our product and engineering team, this is where things get exciting.</strong> In audit, a plausible answer isn't good enough. Every output has to be explainable and traceable back to its source. We've just launched a brand new agentic platform, Alwin by DataSnipper. AI agents running in the cloud across hundreds of documents at once, reasoning across PDF, Word and Excel, with a full audit trail behind every step. There are lots of greenfield problems ahead, and real room to shape what we build and how we build it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">And we build at scale. More than <strong>600,000 professionals across 3,000+ organizations in 175 countries</strong> rely on DataSnipper, including Fortune 500 companies, government agencies and all Big Four audit firms. In 2025 alone, the DataSnipper platform delivered more than <strong>$1.4 billion in productivity savings to is customers</strong>. Backed by a $100 million Series B led by Index Ventures, at a $1 billion valuation, and as proud members of 1% for the Planet, we care about how we grow, not just how fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you want to build AI that professionals trust with work that really matters, <em>this is your chance to help shape the future of audit and finance and do the best work of your career along the way.</em></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What you'll own</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define the correct answer, and the reasoning behind it, for the procedures our agents perform</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interpret ISAs and NV COS (IFRS for reporting matters; US GAAS and PCAOB where relevant) into requirements engineers can build against</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create realistic audit cases with AI tools, including documents, workpapers, exceptions and judgement calls, and review every one</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review agent output against those cases, and find misapplied standards, weak reasoning and conclusions that wouldn't pass partner review</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn recurring errors into findings product and engineering can fix</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Give a clear, evidenced view on whether a capability is ready for live engagements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review methodology content from partners and our own teams, with versioning, approval and documented changes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track changes in standards and inspection findings, and explain what they mean for the product</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Teach product and engineering how audit work is actually done, including how firms differ</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with customers and content partners when the work requires it</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll bring</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A professional qualification: RA, AA, CPA, CA, ACA, ACCA or equivalent</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience as an Audit Manager: setting the approach, reviewing others' work, clearing review notes and defending conclusions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recent experience across several clients and industries</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of ISQM 1 and how firms document and review audit work</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Regular use of AI tools, and a clear sense of how they fail</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Precise writing: people without your training will build from what you write</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Patience for detail: line-by-line review, and real time spent on a single conclusion</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nice to have: </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want to use your audit expertise on hard problems in AI: judgement, evidence and review</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'd rather change how audit work is done than automate how it's done today</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You've built something yourself, such as a tool, prototype or workflow, to fix a slow process</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You stay with open-ended problems until the answer holds up</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What this role is not</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not product management. You shape what ships, but you don't own the roadmap</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not implementation or customer success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not volume work. AI produces the volume; you decide what's right</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Recruitment steps</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Recruiter screen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview with an Audit Expert</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Assessment interview</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final conversations with the people you would work alongside</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>At DataSnipper, we believe great ideas come from different perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds. We are committed to building an inclusive workplace and providing every candidate with a fair and equitable hiring experience.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Our hiring decisions are merit-based and grounded in the skills, experience, potential, and capabilities relevant to the role.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>We welcome applicants regardless of age, race, ethnici