hat’s open, flat, and inclusive, where curiosity drives us, ownership matters, and everyone has the freedom to challenge ideas and make an impact. Check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://rentman.io/public-roadmap">public roadmap</a> to see what’s coming next!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/user-content/d722c125-c3d1-4d3f-8dbf-08d8ac4ab137/1abd1b97-44fa-4e7c-92e0-d04d95cf059f/Screenshot_2026-07-22_at_17.03.37.png" /></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Mission of this role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thousands of rental companies run their business on Rentman, and many of them depend on it talking smoothly to the rest of their stack: accounting packages, webshops, calendars, and our public API. When an integration breaks, invoices don’t sync, bookings go missing, and customers notice fast.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Senior QA Specialist for the Integrations team, you make sure every release reaches those customers without regressions. You own the team’s test strategy and lead the move from manual release-day testing to an automated, shift-left suite. This is a role with real ownership: you shape how the team thinks about quality, and you grow the practice as our integrations platform grows.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What you'll do</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Join refinement with the Integrations team and write Gherkin (Given/When/Then) acceptance specs that developers turn into tests</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Test new integrations and API changes end to end: our side, the partner’s side, and everything that can go wrong between them (auth, rate limits, partial syncs, retries, data mapping)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Explore beyond the acceptance criteria to find edge cases, and file clear, reproducible bug reports in Jira</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain automated tests in TypeScript, with API and contract tests alongside Playwright E2E tests, and review the tests developers write in pull requests</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the daily automated regression run in GitHub Actions: triage failures the same day and fix flaky tests at the root cause, including ones caused by unreliable third-party sandboxes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run release-day regression and the OWASP ZAP security scan, and give a clear go / no-go call</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Migrate the remaining legacy tests and decide what’s worth automating and what stays manual</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coach developers so they own their tests, and organise QA days with the other product teams</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><div style="text-align:left"><img style="max-width:100%" src="https://app.ashbyhq.com/api/images/user-content/d722c125-c3d1-4d3f-8dbf-08d8ac4ab137/3c95dc18-9519-4446-b1af-13a805537681/Screenshot_2026-07-23_at_10.38.46.png" /></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What we are looking for </strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in QA on web applications</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience testing REST APIs and integrations with external systems (Postman, Playwright API testing or similar), including authentication flows like OAuth and webhooks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 2 years writing and maintaining test automation in code (Playwright, Cypress or Selenium, ideally TypeScript/JavaScript), not only record-and-play tools</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong exploratory testing skills, with bug reports developers can act on without follow-up questions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ve defined a test strategy (what to automate, what to test manually, coverage), not only executed test cases</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience running automated tests in CI (GitHub Actions or similar)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You get developers to adopt new habits through pairing, good examples and clear specs, not by policing</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to haves</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with complex B2B SaaS, ideally with a public API or integration marketplace</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contract testing (e.g. Pact) or mocking third-party services</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Playwright specifically, and Gherkin / BDD</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading a shift-left change</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Testing integrations with accounting or finance software</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Basic security testing (e.g. OWASP ZAP)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h1><strong>What you’ll get </strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary based on experience, plus 8% holiday allowance</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A results-based bonus based on company performance (up to a full 13th month's salary)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 vacation days to recharge</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Earn an extra day of PTO for each year at Rentman, from your second anniversary up to five years.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A 4-week paid sabbatical after 5 years to go on an adventure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible WFH policy &amp; work from anywhere for 4 weeks a year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension plan through BrightPensioen</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An annual training budget to grow your skills</p></li><li><p style="min-